","id":1503248,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502231-feel-free-to-gush#post1502231\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Vent and Gush are the new hate/love threads, I guess. Let's keep the politics out of this one as well.<br /> <br /> To get us started, I don't think I've ever mentioned how lucky I am with how pleasant my journey so far into transitioning has gone, socially speaking. There are parts of Colorado that aren't the friendliest on the subject, and I happen to live in one city you would really expect to be unfriendly-but I've never really gotten any guff or confrontations about. Most people have actually been not only accepting of it, but rather complimentary. Sure, some people are upset, but they keep it to themselves. I've also got some great friends who provide me lots of encouragment and advice, and while my family doesn't really approve, they've nevertheless have also been free with advice and gifts that's been legitimately helpful. I was really expecting to run into a lot of problems, and I'm not writing it off as a possibility, but I really appreciate how smooth it's been.</div> </div> </div> </div>Really happy for you \ud83d\ude42. I\u2019m off today so just chillin. That\u2019s worth gushing about lol.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Amethyst is my birthstone. She/they.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst","name":"Amethyst","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatar