er","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-25T12:41:44-07:00","id":1509618,"title":"","content":"I have to say that I'm enjoying the back lash that Netflix is getting with the Cleoptra &quot;documentary&quot; where they trying claim she was black despite 2,000 years of coins, statues and descriptions of her that say otherwise. Race swapping a fictional character is one thing, but doing it to a historical figure is another kettle of fish.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-25T15:58:35-07:00","id":1509636,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502231-feel-free-to-gush?p=1509618#post1509618\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have to say that I'm enjoying the back lash that Netflix is getting with the Cleoptra &quot;documentary&quot; where they trying claim she was black despite 2,000 years of coins, statues and descriptions of her that say otherwise. Race swapping a fictional character is one thing, but doing it to a historical figure is another kettle of fish.</div> </div> </div> </div>THat time where everyone was enamored by Hamilton was probably an interesting time to know you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-25T16:04:19-07:00","id":1509637,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502231-feel-free-to-gush?p=1509636#post1509636\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> THat time where everyone was enamored by Hamilton was probably an interesting time to know you.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the difference -and I'm only speculating, since I've never seen it- was that Hamilton went into it with that being a who specific <i>thing</i> for the show. All the Founding Fathers were specifically cast as non-caucasian actors, weren't they? Whereas changing <i>only</i> Cleopatra (again, me speculating, since I know nothing about this show/documentary/whatever) is... weird. Doubly so if it's meant to be a documentary.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-25T18:24:46-07:00","id":1509669,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502231-feel-free-to-gush?p=1509636#post1509636\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> THat time where everyone was enamored by Hamilton was probably an interesting time to know you.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's a big difference. With Hamilton, that was done as a stylistic choice to draw attention to the hypocrisy that the founders of the US were involved in, and the idea that they didn't believe that &quot;All Men Are Created Equal.&quot; Also it's important to note that Hamilton the musical wasn't trying to claim historical accuracy, nor was the musical trying to peddle the idea that Hamilton was a black man or anything like that. This &quot;documentary&quot; though <i>is</i> attempting to present the case that Cleopatra was actually a black woman, which is obviously complete BS. If Netflix released a documentary about Genghis Khan claiming that he wasn't ethnic Mongolian but was actually, I don't know, Japanese or Arabic or something, I imagine you would see similar pushback.<br /> <br /> In the end it's the difference between using and reframing a historical event or persona to tell a new story, and changing fundamental facts about a historical figure and then presenting those ideas as true. Hamilton wasn't trying to rewrite history, but it appears that Cleopatra is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-25T19:45:22-07:00","id":1509678,"title":"","content":"How do you even race swap someone that died long before our very modern concepts of race?<br /> <br /> If you want to get into the actual history: Cleopatra herself played up her Greek-ness to Romans, and her Egyptian-ness to her subjects (she was one of the few members of her dynasty to actually be fluent in Egyptian). Keep in mind in none of these would be be &quot;white&quot; like many of the women that have played her in the past; the marble statues and busts of her are white because marble is white,and we know those would have been painted; the basalt statues of her to display to Egyptians were black because basalt is black. Coins don't let you show skin color. There is a single painting of her that we know is actually supposed to be her shows her with olive skin, and it also difficult because it follows the Roman tradition of mixing imagery (she's depicted as Venus, and her son as Cupid, in the painting).<br /> <br /> We no nothing about her mother's ancestry.<br /> <br /> The Netflix show also cast a half-black/half-white light skinned woman to play her.<br /> <br /> It's also important to remember a huge amount of the backlash is from the modern Egyptian government's attempts to claim ancient and classic Egyptian history as something that belongs to Arab culture; which is far more absurd than the idea that Cleopatra might have had some dark-skinned folks in her ancestry. Cleopatra wasn't an Arab (though she was at least partially Persian!), but the same bad-faith actors trying to promote a biased version of history are complaining whenever Arabs don't get to control the depiction of Egyptian history long before Arabs took over the area.<br /> <br /> Frankly, any depiction of Cleopatra as anything over that mixed-ancestry is false to history. So good on Netflix for casting someone of mixed-ancestry instead of caving to people that want to try to claim her for their own ancestry despite coming from a period were people didn't care about &quot;race mixing&quot; and we know she had multiple ancestries.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-25T20:13:06-07:00","id":1509679,"title":"","content":"I'll tap out of that discussion. My knowledge of Cleopatra can be summed up with &quot;Egyptian monarch, one of many using that name, part of the Ptolomaic Dynasty, strong Macedonian-Greek heritage/cultural influence&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-25T20:24:00-07:00","id":1509680,"title":"","content":"We've seen murals and pictures from ancient Egypt. They depicted themselves as having brown skin, not white skin or black skin. There are murals with people who do have black skin and white skin, but they are notably rare and usually depicted in the role of slaves. Egyptians weren't Arabic, of course, but in terms of skin color, ancient Egyptians portrayed themselves in artwork as having skin color closer to Arabs than Nubians. And notably the 25th Dynasty was black, having been formed when the Kush conquered Egypt. And murals and statues from that time period definitely show that they were black Africans, unlike the Egyptian Dynasties that came before or after, or the Greek Dynasty we saw even later.<br /> <br /> We also know a lot about Cleopatra's lineage - the Ptolomy Dynasty was so inbred its family tree was basically just the trunk. She was more Greek than Egyptian and definitely not black in the idea of what we, modern day people think of as black. The idea that she was black just isn't historically correct. If this Netflix show is simply presenting the story of Cleopatra with a black actor, in the same way that Hamilton portrayed Hamilton with a black actor, that's cool. But if it's trying to present the idea that Cleopatra was black as a historical fact, then that isn't accurate. It would be about as accurate as claiming that Alexander the Great was actually ethnic Han Chinese.<br /> <br /> Again, if people want to do that as an artistic reinterpretation, that's awesome. But presenting something as historical fact when when it isn't accurate, well, I think it's a good thing to call it out as wrong, even if it has good intentions or what have you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":741,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","user":"AnubisXy","date":". 04-25-2023, 11:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-25T20:40:16-07:00","id":1509683,"title":"","content":"Lets be clear, this is the woman they cast:<br /> <br /> <img title=\"image.png\" data-tempid=\"temp_1191_1682480378023_690\" data-align=\"none\" data-size=\"full\" loading=\"lazy\" border=\"0\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=1191\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=1191\" data-thumb-url=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=1191&amp;type=thumb\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"image.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment thumbnail js-need-data-att-update js-lightbox-participant\" itemprop=\"image\"/>\u200b<br /> <br /> Edit: <a href=\"https://www.imdb.com/name/nm7857440/mediaviewer/rm1156100097?ref_=nmmi_mi_all_pbl_5\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.imdb.com/name/nm7857440/...i_mi_all_pbl_5</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":617,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","user":"Heavy Arms","date":". 04-26-2023, 01:55 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-25T21:09:29-07:00","id":1509685,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar617_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"617\" data-vbnamecard=\"617\">Heavy Arms</a> Can't see that picture.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-26T02:46:56-07:00","id":1509701,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502231-feel-free-to-gush?p=1509678#post1509678\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How do you even race swap someone that died long before our very modern concepts of race?<br /> <br /> If you want to get into the actual history: Cleopatra herself played up her Greek-ness to Romans, and her Egyptian-ness to her subjects (she was one of the few members of her dynasty to actually be fluent in Egyptian). Keep in mind in none of these would be be &quot;white&quot; like many of the women that have played her in the past; the marble statues and busts of her are white because marble is white,and we know those would have been painted; the basalt statues of her to display to Egyptians were black because basalt is black. Coins don't let you show skin color. There is a single painting of her that we know is actually supposed to be her shows her with olive skin, and it also difficult because it follows the Roman tradition of mixing imagery (she's depicted as Venus, and her son as Cupid, in the painting).<br /> <br /> We no nothing about her mother's ancestry.<br /> <br /> The Netflix show also cast a half-black/half-white light skinned woman to play her.<br /> <br /> It's also important to remember a huge amount of the backlash is from the modern Egyptian government's attempts to claim ancient and classic Egyptian history as something that belongs to Arab culture; which is far more absurd than the idea that Cleopatra might have had some dark-skinned folks in her ancestry. Cleopatra wasn't an Arab (though she was at least partially Persian!), but the same bad-faith actors trying to promote a biased version of history are complaining whenever Arabs don't get to control the depiction of Egyptian history long before Arabs took over the area.<br /> <br /> Frankly, any depiction of Cleopatra as anything over that mixed-ancestry is false to history. So good on Netflix for casting someone of mixed-ancestry instead of caving to people that want to try to claim her for their own ancestry despite coming from a period were people didn't care about &quot;race mixing&quot; and we know she had multiple ancestries.</div> </div> </div> </div>Totally with you on this. At the end of the day, what Cleopatra really looked like can only be a guess. So my gut-reaction to this is just a big &quot;Who cares...&quot;<br /> <br /> From what Jada Pinkett-Smith (as executive producer) and Tina Gharavi (as director) have written it seems like they went for a more afrocentric perspective on Cleopatra and ancient Egypt because the bigger series that Cleopatra is a part of is called African Queens. So we know through what lens they approach the whole thing. Of course, though, that will ruffle some feathers with Egypt that as a national project has its own particular view on its history. But it's a Netflix-documentary and hey, I have no doubt that it will at least still be better than Ancient Aliens (their take probably would be that since Cleopatra's ancestry on her mother's side wasn't known, she could've been half-alien...).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-26T05:11:42-07:00","id":1509705,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502231-feel-free-to-gush?p=1509701#post1509701\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Totally with you on this. At the end of the day, what Cleopatra really looked like can only be a guess. So my gut-reaction to this is just a big &quot;Who cares...&quot;<br /> <br /> From what Jada Pinkett-Smith (as executive producer) and Tina Gharavi (as director) have written it seems like they went for a more afrocentric perspective on Cleopatra and ancient Egypt because the bigger series that Cleopatra is a part of is called African Queens. So we know through what lens they approach the whole thing. Of course, though, that will ruffle some feathers with Egypt that as a national project has its own particular view on its history. But it's a Netflix-documentary and hey, I have no doubt that it will at least still be better than Ancient Aliens (their take probably would be that since Cleopatra's ancestry on her mother's side wasn't known, she could've been half-alien...).</div> </div> </div> </div>Totally agree with you and <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar617_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"617\" data-vbnamecard=\"617\">Heavy Arms</a>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Amethyst is my birthstone. She/they.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst","name":"Amethyst","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-26T08:55:31-07:00","id":1509731,"title":"","content":"Tomorrow I get the news of how good the results were of my gum graft and I'm quite hopeful and I can eat on both sides again.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-26T08:58:20-07:00","id":1509733,"title":"","content":"Cleo has been depicted on coins, statues and we have detailed descriptions from Caeser, Mark Anthony and numerous others and she is depicted with much lighter skin and history matters and changing things to make political points or to feel better about yourselves is wrong. That's my two bits.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-26T09:22:17-07:00","id":1509737,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502231-feel-free-to-gush?p=1509733#post1509733\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Cleo has been depicted on coins, statues and we have detailed descriptions from Caeser, Mark Anthony and numerous others and she is depicted with much lighter skin and history matters and changing things to make political points or to feel better about yourselves is wrong. That's my two bits.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar617_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"617\" data-vbnamecard=\"617\">Heavy Arms</a> mentioned that. So she portrayed herself as more Greek to one portion of Egypt and more Egyptian to the rest. And a lot of Royals in that region did that. Mithridates (I forget which number he was... the one who famously drank a little bit of poison each day to build up immunity) did something similar. Because the Ptolemy-dynasty that was in control of Egypt at that time was a result of the post-Alexander-The-Great-period (that whole period where the Diadochi were killing each other to figure out who controlled what of the regions that Alexander The Great had conquered).<br /> <br /> Personally, the thing I would focus on there is less on which person had what skin-color and more on how interconnected this ancient world already was. There's a lot to say about how Cleopatra and Egypt came to be such a power-player in the Mediterranean. And then when you get to Cleopatra and Caesar, there's a lot to say about Roman politics (and their expansionist ambitions). Also, it's Caesar... so that gives it a whole other wrinkle, of course.<br /> <br /> That's another reason why this whole thing just elicits this &quot;Who cares...&quot; from me. There's so much going on there that I don't think Cleopatra's actual skin color is that big of a deal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-26T13:15:12-07:00","id":1509770,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502231-feel-free-to-gush?p=1509733#post1509733\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Cleo has been depicted on coins, statues and we have detailed descriptions from Caeser, Mark Anthony and numerous others and she is depicted with much lighter skin and history matters and changing things to make political points or to feel better about yourselves is wrong. That's my two bits.</div> </div> </div> </div>OK so:<br /> <br /> 1) It's a gush thread, not the vent thread. You wanted to gush about other people venting, and the sources of that venting deserve interrogation. If all you want to do is vent about how historical figures are treated in media... we have a thread for that.<br /> <br /> 2) Arc's point about Hamilton is more relevant and harder to dismiss if your core point is that people shouldn't be messing around in <b>art</b> for political, or representational reasons.<br /> <br /> 3) The backlash you were gushing over was not fueled by people that share your values here. You're siding with people that want to change history for political, social, and religious reasons. And worse, unlike the artists they selectively rail against, they're government officials trying to censor art they don't like; not historians trying to preserve the truth.<br /> <br /> If you really care about history like this, the backlash against the show is far worse for history than people challenging it with historically questionable art. I'll gush over artists standing up to government propagandists despite their artistic liberties with history any day.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-26T16:48:02-07:00","id":1509795,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502231-feel-free-to-gush?p=1509770#post1509770\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2) Arc's point about Hamilton is more relevant and harder to dismiss if your core point is that people shouldn't be messing around in <b>art</b> for political, or representational reasons.<br /> <br /> If you really care about history like this, the backlash against the show is far worse for history than people challenging it with historically questionable art. I'll gush over artists standing up to government propagandists despite their artistic liberties with history any day.</div> </div> </div> </div>Is this show simply intended to be an artistic reimagining of who Cleopatra was, or is the goal of the creators to essentially rewrite history by convincing people that historians are wrong and Cleopatra wasn't a Greek/Persian? Ultimately there's a difference between something that is an artistic and playful reimagining of history, and something that purports itself to be historical fact. From the way the show has been presented, it seems like it's the latter case.<br /> <br /> I do think that people should cool it until the show is out and it can be judged on its own merits, but if people are drawing the wrong conclusion as to the what the show is about and the goal's of the creators, to some degree that is the fault of creators for advertising the show in the way that they have.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-26T17:29:41-07:00","id":1509803,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502231-feel-free-to-gush?p=1509795#post1509795\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> From the way the show has been presented, it seems like it's the latter case.</div> </div> </div> </div>Where is the show's promotion itself saying that?<br /> <br /> The show's producer has stated directly that part of the casting choice was to help spark people to challenge their preconceptions about how Cleopatra's story has been told in the past; not that it's about trying to make a specific claim about Cleopatra's skin color as historical fact. The idea is to get you to think about the factual events presented in a different light than some old (and even most historians will agree) very off-base preconceptions about her role in history.<br /> <br /> The show is sold as being purposefully provocative. Again, the Hamilton comparison is very apt. The casting is meant to get people to think about history in a different way, that can expand our understanding, or get people to pay attention to history they didn't think was relevant to them before seeing in presented in such a &quot;disruptive&quot; way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-26T18:14:36-07:00","id":1509807,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502231-feel-free-to-gush?p=1509770#post1509770\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1) It's a gush thread, not the vent thread. You wanted to gush about other people venting, and the sources of that venting deserve interrogation. If all you want to do is vent about how historical figures are treated in media... we have a thread for that.</div> </div> </div> </div>In mild fairness, this started on what could be understood as a vent. I was more waiting to see how they personally squared the circle before coming down on any particular subject, but I get the read.<br /> <br /> Of course, now that we've applied pi to the picture, I feel pretty safe in stating that I'm disinclined to agree with the original complaint (for pretty much every reason raised by Heavy Arms, a general tiredness of how Cleopatra's story is usually mistold*, and a deeper tiredness with white outrage in general) and by contrast I'm quite looking forward to Netflix flipping the bird and going ahead anyways, and I wish the show much success for it.<br /> <br /> *If a not-white Cleopatra has people gnashing their teeth, I pity the dentists if they also lean into how she was more of a gifted conversationalist than a seductress.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-26T19:22:14-07:00","id":1509818,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502231-feel-free-to-gush?p=1509807#post1509807\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">*If a not-white Cleopatra has people gnashing their teeth, I pity the dentists if they also lean into how she was more of a gifted conversationalist than a seductress.</div> </div> </div> </div>Uh. Are people still taking Octavian's propaganda at face value?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-26T19:38:17-07:00","id":1509819,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502231-feel-free-to-gush?p=1509818#post1509818\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Uh. Are people still taking Octavian's propaganda at face value?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think most people even know how much of what we know about Cleopatra comes from someone who was invested in minimalizing her.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-26T20:12:08-07:00","id":1509826,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502231-feel-free-to-gush?p=1509803#post1509803\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Where is the show's promotion itself saying that?<br /> <br /> The show's producer has stated directly that part of the casting choice was to help spark people to challenge their preconceptions about how Cleopatra's story has been told in the past; not that it's about trying to make a specific claim about Cleopatra's skin color as historical fact. The idea is to get you to think about the factual events presented in a different light than some old (and even most historians will agree) very off-base preconceptions about her role in history.<br /> <br /> The show is sold as being purposefully provocative. Again, the Hamilton comparison is very apt. The casting is meant to get people to think about history in a different way, that can expand our understanding, or get people to pay attention to history they didn't think was relevant to them before seeing in presented in such a &quot;disruptive&quot; way.</div> </div> </div> </div>The whole, &quot;I don't care what you learned in school, Cleopatra was black,&quot; tagline and other moments like Jada Smith (the producer) making saying that it's her goal for her series African Queens is to to showcase black queens in order to offer black girls representation. Again, some people have taken this to mean that the show will be presenting the idea that Cleopatra wasn't a woman of Greek/Persian descent.<br /> <br /> I don't think people have an issue with the idea of reframing or disrupting history, but there are problems when people begin presenting things that aren't true as fact. That starts to get into misinformation, where people are being led to believe that something is true when it isn't. I don't think that applies to Hamilton - nobody is going to see it and believe that Hamilton was actually black. But depending on how this documentary presents itself, people may come away with certain ideas about Cleopatra that aren't historically accurate. Generally speaking, documentaries and musicals are generally held to different standards as far as artistic license goes, people are going into a documentary with the idea that it's going to be dealing more with fact than with fiction.<br /> <br /> That's why I think it's important to wait and see what's in the documentary before judging, but based on some of the material we've seen, it appears that it is going to be presenting the idea that Cleopatra was not a woman of Greek/Persian descent. If that's the case, then I hope it will include moments where it makes it clear that this is an artistic reinterpreation of who Cleopatra really was and that she wasn't the person she's being depicted as.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-26T20:29:59-07:00","id":1509829,"title":"","content":"Re: Cleopatra - What HA and Arc said.<br /> <br /> Re: the actual purpose of this thread - Pathfinder is finally getting rid of alignment and I fucking love it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-26T20:42:15-07:00","id":1509831,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Second Chances</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502231-feel-free-to-gush?p=1509829#post1509829\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Re: the actual purpose of this thread - Pathfinder is finally getting rid of alignment and I fucking love it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Praise the sun. Alignment-based Outsiders were the only cool part of that sub-system, and they'll mostly work fine without it. Otherwise it's just a stupid sacred cow.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-26T22:30:19-07:00","id":1509835,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502231-feel-free-to-gush?p=1509826#post1509826\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The whole, &quot;I don't care what you learned in school, Cleopatra was black,&quot; tagline...</div> </div> </div> </div>Where is that every the &quot;tagline&quot; of the show? It's a quote of a quote in a snippet of an interview as one part of the trailer when it touches on how Cleopatra has become an icon in modern culture (which is a fair place to discuss the black-Cleopatra cultural movement).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> ...and other moments like Jada Smith (the producer) making saying that it's her goal for her series African Queens is to to showcase black queens in order to offer black girls representation. </div> </div> </div>Executive producer. And this is also the second entry in the series, with the first focusing more strongly on Jada Smith's original intentions (I doubt most people know who Nzinga Mbande is even though the first entry was about her), but got very little coverage... the idea of moving on to a less black and more popular figure to get more focus on the series in general is the kind of things that happens in TV all the time.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Again, some people have taken this to mean that the show will be presenting the idea that Cleopatra wasn't a woman of Greek/Persian descent. </div> </div> </div>They say she is in the trailer.<br /> <br /> Who's actually made a big complaint about this other than the Egyptian Cultural Ministry? I can't find anyone really leaning into this accusation about the show other than them (and their history with who they complain about is exceedingly hypocritical).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I don't think people have an issue with the idea of reframing or disrupting history, but there are problems when people begin presenting things that aren't true as fact. </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> That's why I think it's important to wait and see what's in the documentary before judging,... </div> </div> </div>If you're going to wait to judge, can you wait to judge? Because it doesn't feel like you're waiting; just hiding behind some JAQing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-26T23:17:46-07:00","id":1509839,"title":"","content":"Can I formally request this discussion either move to it's own thread, the Vent thread, or be dropped? It really isn't in the spirit of this thread.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-27T14:55:26-07:00","id":1509895,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502231-feel-free-to-gush?p=1509819#post1509819\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't think most people even know how much of what we know about Cleopatra comes from someone who was invested in minimalizing her.</div> </div> </div> </div>True people don't know that Cleo was a skilled and capable leader who used the power of the Roman empire not once but twice to increase her hold on ancient Egypt and increased the holding of her family line back to the levels that the founder of the line was able to create.<br /> <br /> Her critics like Augustus and others would like to attribute her as a mystic rather then the fact she was a skilled political operator in her own right.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-27T15:03:17-07:00","id":1509897,"title":"","content":"Anyone looking forward to a possible Highlander remake with Henry Cavill? It sounds interesting and I think he would do a good job as Conner McColud and I wouldn't mind it at all if he couldn't do the accent right.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-27T17:09:48-07:00","id":1509908,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502231-feel-free-to-gush?p=1509897#post1509897\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anyone looking forward to a possible Highlander remake with Henry Cavill? It sounds interesting and I think he would do a good job as Conner McColud and I wouldn't mind it at all if he couldn't do the accent right.</div> </div> </div> </div>I need a trailer. Chad Stahleski is pretty reliable as getting into the action and worldbuilding that Highlander needs, and I'm sold on Bautista as the Kurgan, but Henry Cavill himself does nothing for me, and I'm a little worried it's gonna be more serious about it's worldbuilding and with it's tone than it's themes. Call out the flaws with the original where it stands, they hold, but that movie's particular way of taking it's themes seriously but was looser and even sillier with it's characters is a big part of the reason why it had lasting appeal.<br /> <br /> Also if it's not R, then what are we even doing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-28T12:10:10-07:00","id":1509978,"title":"","content":"Bauista as the Kurgan would be interesting and it would be interesting how he would play the monster against how Clancy Brown did in the original. I hope he is up to the task as he has some pretty big shoes to fill in that role. Mr. Brown did a masterful job in that role. As it stands there is no trailer for it yet and it's still in the starting phases right now and I hope it goes through.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-28T12:14:10-07:00","id":1509980,"title":"","content":"I'm sort of looking forward to the Renfield movie with Nicolas Cage as Dracula and I know it will be crazy as only he could do it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-29T07:20:05-07:00","id":1510081,"title":"","content":"Renfield was a lot of fun. My friend and I sure enjoyed it.<br /> <br /> Made me wonder if Cage could play a good Joker in some Batman movie.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24473-willowfang","name":"Willowfang","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24473_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"92"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-29T09:43:15-07:00","id":1510098,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Willowfang</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502231-feel-free-to-gush?p=1510081#post1510081\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Renfield was a lot of fun. My friend and I sure enjoyed it.<br /> <br /> Made me wonder if Cage could play a good Joker in some Batman movie.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes Cage could make a good older looking Joker and from his work in Willy's Wonderland, Mandy, Faceoff and others cliched it for me. We just have to find a good actor to play an aged Batman to hold his own. That reminds me that some point in the future I should watch the Robert Patterson version of Batman and hopefully be pleasantly surprised.<br /> <br /> I'm old enough to remember when eyebrows were raised when Michael Keaton was cast as Batman and he was known for his roles of Johnny Dangerously, Mr. Mom &amp; Beetlejuice at the time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":27361,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","user":"Lysander","date":". 05-06-2023, 12:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-06T06:36:15-07:00","id":1510881,"title":"","content":"Patterson's Batman was pretty solid. The movie was rather low-key and subdued. But I was happy to have seen it at the theater. I wouldn't mind another 1 or 2 Patterson Batman movies.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24473-willowfang","name":"Willowfang","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24473_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"92"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-06T09:22:11-07:00","id":1510887,"title":"","content":"I'll most likely check it out in the future when my genre fatique is gone and I knew it was bad when a Batman movie wasn't enough to spur any desire and I'm a big Dark Knight fan.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-06T11:46:57-07:00","id":1510901,"title":"","content":"1) Spring is the best season. The sun is, at this time, neither abandoning us to freeze nor attempting to burn us all alive, which is great. I don't tend to get hay fever, so the flowers everywhere are lovely (condolences to those that do though), and the birds screaming musical obscenities at each other makes for nice ambience.<br /> <br /> 2) Standing on a cliff overlooking the ocean is possibly the best emotional decompression around for me. The wind blows, the waves crash, the world spreads out below, the sun shines down on you. Somewhere out there the moon pulls the tides and the solar system turns and shit, and everything just bleeds out leaving me empty and peaceful.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><sup><i>Prone to hyperbole</i></sup>","edited":{"userid":26836,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26836-rhywbeth","user":"Rhywbeth","date":". 05-06-2023, 03:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26836-rhywbeth","name":"Rhywbeth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26836_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"377"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-08T05:11:56-07:00","id":1511068,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rhywbeth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502231-feel-free-to-gush?p=1510901#post1510901\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1) Spring is the best season. The sun is, at this time, neither abandoning us to freeze nor attempting to burn us all alive, which is great. I don't tend to get hay fever, so the flowers everywhere are lovely (condolences to those that do though), and the birds screaming musical obscenities at each other makes for nice ambience.<br /> <br /> 2) Standing on a cliff overlooking the ocean is possibly the best emotional decompression around for me. The wind blows, the waves crash, the world spreads out below, the sun shines down on you. Somewhere out there the moon pulls the tides and the solar system turns and shit, and everything just bleeds out leaving me empty and peaceful.</div> </div> </div> </div>Went for a hike yesterday at Big Bend. Was really cool to stand on the cliff looking at endless see of green with all the smells of just grown flowers around! Definitely love me some Spring, not too hot yet but just good enough to adventure outside! [Upd.] Okay now it's way too hot there, went for another quick trail last Saturday. Signed for a cowboy shooting event recently, gonna be practicing at local <a href=\"https://range.gritrsports.com/\" target=\"_blank\">gun range</a> in upcoming weeks <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27970,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27970-oharaj","user":"OharaJ","date":". 05-18-2023, 07:14 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27970-oharaj","name":"OharaJ","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-16T09:03:00-07:00","id":1511809,"title":"","content":"It's a great feeling that things you liked as a child are still good to watch or read still hold up well as an adult when you review them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-17T01:39:21-07:00","id":1511848,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502231-feel-free-to-gush?p=1511809#post1511809\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's a great feeling that things you liked as a child are still good to watch or read still hold up well as an adult when you review them.</div> </div> </div> </div>I used to unironically love old Mario bros movie. In restrospect, I was really wrong <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Also next week my vacation is starting(yay). Gonna pick up some gear at Gritroutdoors(one of my fav online sports store <a href=\"https://gritroutdoors.com/\" target=\"_blank\">https://gritroutdoors.com/</a>\u200b ) and probably do a 3 days hike at Big Bend into visiting my uncle's hunting lodge near Dallas. Can't wait already!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27970,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27970-oharaj","user":"OharaJ","date":". 05-26-2023, 05:16 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27970-oharaj","name":"OharaJ","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-17T11:10:59-07:00","id":1511889,"title":"","content":"I\u2019m Graduated! I now have a Bachelor\u2019s of Physics. Now to try and find a job and pay off those debts. That\u2019s the easy part, right?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-17T15:17:37-07:00","id":1511923,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>OharaJ</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502231-feel-free-to-gush?p=1511848#post1511848\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I used to unironically love old Mario bros movie. In restrospect, I was really wrong <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>That's all right as I thought Highlander 2 The Regenade version was cool where they removed the alien angle and made residents of an ancient high-tech feudal past with hover ships and time travel .<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Oh to be young and foolish.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":27361,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","user":"Lysander","date":". 05-17-2023, 06:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-18T04:15:50-07:00","id":1511997,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502231-feel-free-to-gush?p=1511889#post1511889\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I\u2019m Graduated! I now have a Bachelor\u2019s of Physics. Now to try and find a job and pay off those debts. That\u2019s the easy part, right?</div> </div> </div> </div>At least you have a usable degree compared to many <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Worst case scenario you would need to adapt a bit if it's not in your direct field<br /> Congrats though!<br /> <br /> Regarding gushing: I've been practicing for marathon for over 2 years now and still not there... Gonna be working more but it's a bit sad at this point(also I think I need new running shoes, probably going to get myself topo shoes from <a href=\"https://rununited.com/topo-athletic/\" target=\"_blank\">https://rununited.com/topo-athletic/</a>\u200b again, those are really good)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27970,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27970-oharaj","user":"OharaJ","date":". 10-13-2023, 03:08 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27970-oharaj","name":"OharaJ","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-18T08:45:07-07:00","id":1512017,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502231-feel-free-to-gush?p=1511889#post1511889\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View 