,"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-21T22:27:47-08:00","id":1529138,"title":"","content":"I appreciate and love how quickly the mods get involved in the unfortunate cases where I've felt it was necessary to get them involved.<br /> <br /> And most recently when one of my groups was discussing potential games I brought out my list of WoD and CoD books (splats and sets since my random ownership of a promethean adventure without the promethean book wouldn't help anyone.) There was some minor joking about the fact that the only line on the list I'd made notation on was my refusal to play Wraith. I simply explained that Wraith kind of hits things I deal with via therapy. At which point the joking stopped and it was just a polite request on whether or not I was comfortable explaining what the potential landmine was so it could be avoided in future games. Which I explained and after one asked a clarifying question to make sure they'd understood the details of my explanation the matter was ended. Which I'm very proud of them for doing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-21T22:29:30-08:00","id":1529140,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502231-feel-free-to-gush?p=1528945#post1528945\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I got two new job interviews lined up and I'm feeling incredibly good right now and I should go out to a decent restraurant just to celebrate the good news.</div> </div> </div> </div>Good luck! Unless they've already happened in which case I hope they went well!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-22T12:20:37-08:00","id":1529166,"title":"","content":"Well one will be another group interview which I find more relaxing, but I have to make sure that I stand out from the others who are looking at the same job. The other is the traditional one on one interview that is nerve wracking for sure.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-22T16:38:32-08:00","id":1529178,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amethyst</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502231-feel-free-to-gush?p=1528885#post1528885\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I got married!!! I\u2019m so happy. No need to respond, I just wanted to let you know.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you for the Likes \ud83d\ude0a","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Amethyst is my birthstone. She/they.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst","name":"Amethyst","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-22T17:12:36-08:00","id":1529183,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Matt Corleone</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502231-feel-free-to-gush?p=1529113#post1529113\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I love Westerns</div> </div> </div> </div>You can't go wrong with Westerns. I remember watching many John Wayne films like The Searchers, Chisum, Sons of Katie Elder, Rio Lobo, and many others of his film including Clint Eastwood's films with Pale Rider, Outlaw Josey Wales and Unforgiven being my favorites with my parents. Tombstone, 310 To Yuma and the original Magnificent 7 were good and you got to love spagetti westerns with the late Lee Van Cleef and Eli Wallchi.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":27361,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","user":"Lysander","date":". 01-22-2024, 08:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-30T12:12:15-08:00","id":1529728,"title":"","content":"I'm not lying when I like the somewhat campy Godzilla movies from my childhood.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-04T12:48:15-08:00","id":1529980,"title":"","content":"I can not get enough Nicolas Cage or Christopher Walken films, the more over the top the better in my opionion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-07T06:48:38-08:00","id":1530158,"title":"","content":"I'm currently reading &quot;A Tainted Cup&quot; by Robert Jackson Bennett and that author once again produced an interesting setting with an interesting genre-mix. It's this setting where technology is all plant-based and people &quot;enhance&quot; themselves via genetic modification. And so you have thise empire of all these humans modifying themselves and the environment around them set against the threat of Kaiju-style monsters trying to invade that empire. And it's only because of that threat that the empire grew so quickly because it was only due to these plant-based inhuman improvements that human civilization was able to put up a defense against these Kaiju-monsters that are coming from the ocean.<br /> <br /> That's the setting but the genre of the story the novel is a Sherlockian Whodunnit-mystery that starts with the bizarre murder of a famous general (since it's plant-based, the bizarre murder-weapon is a supernatural seed that made a small tree grow out of the general's head within seconds).<br /> <br /> So far, it seems like yet another really fun novel from Robert Jackson Bennett.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-08T14:24:04-08:00","id":1530315,"title":"","content":"I've been reading the last of the Four Horsemen by Laura Thessily and it's about the final Horseman Death picking up where his siblings left off after they were convinced to stop and give the survivors a chance, but Death is the most important one to convince and is being hounded by a woman named Lazarus who can't die and is curious about that. I'm not much into fantasy romance but I find the story engaging off to stick with it to the end.<br /> <br /> Who says that women can't write fantasy or science fiction is a strange comment for me to hear.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-08T16:25:26-08:00","id":1530325,"title":"","content":"Watched season 2 of Bridgerton the other day. Almost as good as the first season. And I really like the characters, especially Penelope and Eloise.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Amethyst is my birthstone. She/they.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst","name":"Amethyst","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-14T13:17:47-08:00","id":1530843,"title":"","content":"Watched Criminal with actors and actresses like Tommy Lee Jones, Gary Oldman, Kevin Costner, and Gal Gadot and a few good supporting cast that you can rely on with whatever role you give them. The story was not ground breaking but how often do you see a cast like this?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-19T18:06:07-08:00","id":1531159,"title":"","content":"I actually like watching, &quot;The Last of Us&quot;. <br /> <br /> And also, &quot;The Last Kingdom&quot;, which is better than, &quot;Vikings&quot;,","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I have all the power in the world to give you, and all you have to do is beg&quot; -Nix<br /> <br /> &quot;There's thing about being a vampire, Frank; it takes a long fucking time to learn how do all the cool shit&quot;. -Abigail","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2521-iguazu","name":"Iguazu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2521_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"740"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-20T12:56:49-08:00","id":1531208,"title":"","content":"I've been getting into Laura Thessily's series of books and I find them engaging.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-20T13:13:48-08:00","id":1531213,"title":"","content":"I had a really positive interview not to long ago where I got both a phone interview and a in person interview and I was given a tour of the place after it was done. It seemed that I made a very good impression on the people I met and hopefully I will get a call in a few days.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude00","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-22T12:34:37-08:00","id":1531305,"title":"","content":"You have to love it when Space Ice uploads another video on really bad movies or over the top good movies and this time he did Escape From New York with Kurt Russel and made comments of all the movies he had done at that point in time and seeing some of the cool supporting cast like Donald Pleasance, Ernest Borginine, Issac Hayes and Lee Van Cleef seemingly enjoying the roles. Also I found a cool looking Nicolas Cage film and Sudden Death with Van Dam amongst my travels today.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":27361,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","user":"Lysander","date":". 02-22-2024, 05:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-23T08:26:47-08:00","id":1531358,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502231-feel-free-to-gush?p=1531305#post1531305\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You have to love it when Space Ice uploads another video on really bad movies or over the top good movies and this time he did Escape From New York with Kurt Russel and made comments of all the movies he had done at that point in time and seeing some of the cool supporting cast like Donald Pleasance, Ernest Borginine, Issac Hayes and Lee Van Cleef seemingly enjoying the roles. Also I found a cool looking Nicolas Cage film and Sudden Death with Van Dam amongst my travels today.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, a John Carpenter movie <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> ! One of the greats, I would say. Nobody does &quot;genre&quot; like that guy. You have these movies that are very conventional on one hand but then get these very interesting representations. Escape From New York isn't high on my John Carpenter tier-list but it's very John Carpenter. I haven't seen the video but did it get into who John Carpenter considered for the role before Kurt Russell? And how that influenced Kurt's performance in the movie? Because that part is really interesting. And of course, this movie gave us Kurt Russell in &quot;The Thing&quot;.<br /> <br /> Last Christmas when I was at my parents (who have no streaming whatsoever) Escape (etc.) was on TV and I suggested we should watch that. And 30 minutes into the movie my mother said out loud &quot;This movie sucks.&quot;. But the movie is a bit hokey and the production-value isn't so great when it comes to the sets but I think the movie still has some great vibes if you can get on the same wavelength as the movie (and the soundtrack by John Carpenter is great 80s synth).<br /> <br /> I also think the Blank Check podcast did a <a href=\"https://soundcloud.com/griffin-and-david-present/escape-from-new-york-with-karen-han\" target=\"_blank\">great episode</a> on the movie.<br /> <br /> And of course, the thing John Carpenter is most known for these days is his based quotes about not giving a single shit anymore:<br /> <br /> (From an <a href=\"https://variety.com/2023/film/features/john-carpenter-career-interview-director-halloween-the-thing-1235485167/\" target=\"_blank\">interview with Variety</a>)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <i>Did you ever have any dreams of continuing the Laurie Strode \u201cHalloween\u201d story?</i><br /> <br /> Well, I thought after the first one there was no more story. Boy, was I wrong, huh? They kept bringing that thing back. I wrote the second one \u2014 it was out of desperation. Anyway, I thought after that, \u201cLet\u2019s steer this baby away.\u201d I wanted to do different movies every year under the title \u201cHalloween.\u201d So \u201cHalloween III\u201d was that kind of a film. Boy, the audience didn\u2019t like that! \u201cNo, no, no, no! We want our Michael Myers back with a knife!\u201d I thought, \u201cOh God, OK. Well, this is what they want.\u201d<br /> <br /> But then the producers brought back Michael Myers in some storyline. <b>It was great in one sense though. I want to just be real honest about it: They had to pay me every single time they made those movies, and it was wonderful. That\u2019s my favorite kind of experience in Hollywood: I\u2019m on a couch, maybe watching some TV, and I extend my hand and a check arrives and it rubs in my hand. That I\u2019m talented at.</b> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-23T11:51:51-08:00","id":1531372,"title":"","content":"Even better Knightingale is now many of the younger audience are rediscovering some these classic films and are amazed by the passion and skill that people put into them even if they were not big successes when they first came out and seeing what is currently lacking in today's movie industry as fewer people are willing to take risks because it might offend a small group of people on social media.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-23T19:37:13-08:00","id":1531401,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502231-feel-free-to-gush?p=1531372#post1531372\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Even better Knightingale is now many of the younger audience are rediscovering some these classic films and are amazed by the passion and skill that people put into them even if they were not big successes when they first came out and seeing what is currently lacking in today's movie industry as fewer people are willing to take risks because it might offend a small group of people on social media.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ha, I'm not that young anymore. Middle-age is approaching me with terminal velocity <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> . At least, that means I'm in that sweespot where I don't have to get defensive about being young and I'm also not expected to crack self-deprecating jokes about being too old.<br /> <br /> But yeah, John Carpenter is definitely one of those filmmakers who got a critical re-evaluation after the heyday when his work was released. The reception of his movies at the time of their release was very different compared to how they are generally perceived these days. I mean, Roger Ebert was dead-wrong about The Thing in his review, for example, that he wrote at the time of the release. But that's how it goes sometimes...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-24T11:17:42-08:00","id":1531433,"title":"","content":"I'm moving way to fast into middle age and seeing that retirement isn't too far away. To be fair I never paid much attention to film critics even when I was a child as 9 times out 10 that they hated the movies that most people liked or loved films that most found slow and tedious.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":27361,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","user":"Lysander","date":". 02-24-2024, 02:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-26T15:06:08-08:00","id":1531549,"title":"","content":"I finished reading &quot;A Swim In A Pond In The Rain&quot; by George Saunders this weekend and that had been more pleasant and accessible than I expected. It's the lecture of George Saunders (famous short-story-author) doing a lecture on Russian short-stories and this is supposed to be the book-version of that. May favorite was the short-story from Tolstoy called &quot;Master And Man&quot;. Such a great story that highlights storytelling which is all about &quot;show, don't tell&quot;.<br /> <br /> I also read the short Sci-Fi-novel from Nick Harkaway called Titanium Noir. It's more detective-fiction. Just pulled that from my TBR-2023-pile after enjoying the mystery-stuff in A Tainted Cup by Robert Jackson Bennett. It's still a novel with a great sci-fi-concept: There's a miracle-drug which heals even the biggest injury and it reverses aging - the downside...? You grow bigger every time you use it. And so there's a wealthy elite in this setting which are literal giants. But it also highlights that it isn't pleasant being these supposedly immortal giants. But I think the biggest strength isn't that sci-fi-conceit but the writing itself. I listened to the audiobook-version and I think the writing is especially strong if someone reads it out loud. There's a rhythm to the curt dialogues the detective-main-character has with people. And having someone read it out loud to you really emphasizes the rhythm/metric of the text.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-27T09:30:38-08:00","id":1531628,"title":"","content":"AC/DC kicks ass!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer