of what he was like before the war and how he was happy doing research with Skyfire and his fellow seekers and not really caring about the war until his best friend tragically died and Megatron swooped in and recruited him using Starscream grief as a effective tool.<br /> <br /> ThunderCracker is getting more disgusted with himself and his role in the war on Earth and how the humans are getting caught up with the conflict and feeling shame and deserts his fellow cons.<br /> <br /> The Autobots are struggling with a new world and Prime seems to be suffering from PTSD and to be fair all of the Transformers are suffering from it and looking for ways to cope.<br /> <br /> Even better we got to see the Combaticons and the Constructionicons show up and have a good old slug fest.<br /> <br /> All in all I am glad that Image Comics has the licence and hope that they can keep up the good stories.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":27361,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","user":"Lysander","date":". 05-21-2025, 03:05 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-21T16:24:25-07:00","id":1551206,"title":"","content":"I'm actually glad that I have been able to find some good comic book series from Image, Dark Horse, Boom Studio's and even Dynamite comics. I might not follow superhero stuff anymore but there's always a few gems in a mountain of bad stories.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-27T13:57:49-07:00","id":1551317,"title":"","content":"I've really been enjoying <a href=\"https://revolutionspodcast.libsyn.com/\" target=\"_blank\">the recent season of the Revolutions-podcast</a>. For the most recent season, rather than covering a historical revolution the host Mike Duncan wrote a fictional scenario of a future revolution for Martian independence based on revolutions from the past. I especially like the style he chose of acting like a historian for whom the Martian Revolution happened in the past so issues like source-trustworthiness or loss of sources come up as well and you see the contours of tropes from other revolutions when issues like gerontocracy come up.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-28T07:15:04-07:00","id":1551328,"title":"","content":"Just finished reading the new Ravenloft novel Heir of Strahd. It\u2019s a fantastic book. I loved it and I\u2019m really glad I bought it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Amethyst is my birthstone. She/they.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst","name":"Amethyst","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-30T22:36:42-07:00","id":1551358,"title":"","content":"I just finished watching The Ghost Rite Here Rite Now concert DVD and it was awesome and that you don't need to scream incoherently into a microphone to be a good metal singer. In fact in the older groups like Alice Cooper and others had clean vocals that you could hear properly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-30T22:44:31-07:00","id":1551360,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr Gone</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502231-feel-free-to-gush?p=1551120#post1551120\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Did anyone watch the new season of Andor? It was pretty amazing! Episodes 7-9 were especially great, but the whole season was awesome!</div> </div> </div> </div>No I didn't, but I'm glad that you are enjoying it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-31T05:27:38-07:00","id":1551364,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502231-feel-free-to-gush?p=1551358#post1551358\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I just finished watching The Ghost Rite Here Rite Now concert DVD and it was awesome and that you don't need to scream incoherently into a microphone to be a good metal singer. In fact in the older groups like Alice Cooper and others had clean vocals that you could hear properly.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ghost is awesome! And Rite Here Rite Now was pretty cool. I went to see it in a theater when it was released, and I went to one of the concerts from that tour! It was awesome! But yea, Ghost has a great vibe, and I'm really enjoying the new album!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502231-feel-free-to-gush?p=1551360#post1551360\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No I didn't, but I'm glad that you are enjoying it.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's probably top tier Star Wars for me at the moment, especially that newest season! This show treated everything very seriously, and seemed pretty grounded. It was interesting seeing the progression of small rebel cells, and just seeing the universe from a different perspective. Plus, the last few episodes moved nicely into the beginning of Rogue One. I recommend it!<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/\" target=\"_blank\">MrGone's Character Sheets</a><br /> For all your WoD Character Sheet Needs<br /> _________________________________<br /> Buy books &amp; pdfs from DTRPG and support my web site! <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=55414\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a><br /> Support my site on Patreon! <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mrgone\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24-mr-gone","name":"Mr Gone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-31T11:20:27-07:00","id":1551366,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr Gone</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502231-feel-free-to-gush?p=1551364#post1551364\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's probably top tier Star Wars for me at the moment, especially that newest season! This show treated everything very seriously, and seemed pretty grounded. It was interesting seeing the progression of small rebel cells, and just seeing the universe from a different perspective. Plus, the last few episodes moved nicely into the beginning of Rogue One. I recommend it!</div> </div> </div> </div>I've watched it. And as you said, an awesome second season. I thought, like in the first season, the first arc was my least favorite (it's a bit slow... that bit with the resistance fighters in the jungle took a while) but man, this series is just so good. Everything just comes together so well - the performances, the writing, the direction... It's all top-tier. Especially episode 8 about the Ghorman massacre. That's just Star Wars at its best. <br /> <br /> Stellan Skarsgard who played Luthen was great as usual. But I also really enjoyed Ben Mendelsohn as Krennic. You could just see how much fun he had playing a villain for a change. But overall, I don't think there's a single bad actor in the cast. It's just a great show. <br /> <br /> Have you had a chance yet to watch Rogue One again? I liked it when I first saw it but I didn't love it. But having the show as additional context adds so much to the viewing-experience in my opinion. And it's clear that Tony Gilroy was considering the events and details of the movie while making the show. There are so many moments that play so much better for me after I had watched Andor.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-06-01T08:35:21-07:00","id":1551389,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502231-feel-free-to-gush?p=1551366#post1551366\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've watched it. And as you said, an awesome second season. I thought, like in the first season, the first arc was my least favorite (it's a bit slow... that bit with the resistance fighters in the jungle took a while) but man, this series is just so good. Everything just comes together so well - the performances, the writing, the direction... It's all top-tier. Especially episode 8 about the Ghorman massacre. That's just Star Wars at its best.</div> </div> </div> </div>Glad to hear you liked it! Yea, the first arc was a bit slow, but the ending of that arc was crazy! And then it just went up from there. I was really surprised by where it all went! My only complaint is that I was wish we had more! I get why they didn't want to do many more seasons, but I could really have done with then expanding on a few more things. But, I get why they did it this way, and what we did was amazing!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502231-feel-free-to-gush?p=1551366#post1551366\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Stellan Skarsgard who played Luthen was great as usual. But I also really enjoyed Ben Mendelsohn as Krennic. You could just see how much fun he had playing a villain for a change. But overall, I don't think there's a single bad actor in the cast. It's just a great show.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, I totally agree! Everyone did an amazing job. I especially liked Kleya! She was awesome, but what she did in that last arc was pretty amazing!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502231-feel-free-to-gush?p=1551366#post1551366\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Have you had a chance yet to watch Rogue One again? I liked it when I first saw it but I didn't love it. But having the show as additional context adds so much to the viewing-experience in my opinion. And it's clear that Tony Gilroy was considering the events and details of the movie while making the show. There are so many moments that play so much better for me after I had watched Andor.</div> </div> </div> </div>I did! I watched it like a day after I finished Andor and it definitely hit different. I loved the movie already, but the series really added some layers to the movie! It's not quite a different movie now, but the series definitely enhances it! <br /> <br /> Glad to hear you enjoyed it all!<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/\" target=\"_blank\">MrGone's Character Sheets</a><br /> For all your WoD Character Sheet Needs<br /> _________________________________<br /> Buy books &amp; pdfs from DTRPG and support my web site! <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=55414\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a><br /> Support my site on Patreon! <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mrgone\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24-mr-gone","name":"Mr Gone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-06-02T22:32:27-07:00","id":1551435,"title":"","content":"I have been really enjoying getting into the Ghost band Mr. Gone and I can see many of the musical influences that shaped Tobias Forge as a performer and why he is still going strong after nearly twenty years. It's good that he isn't afraid to experiment with his band and not play it safe.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":27361,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","user":"Lysander","date":". 06-03-2025, 01:35 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-06-03T04:29:45-07:00","id":1551440,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502231-feel-free-to-gush?p=1551435#post1551435\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have been really enjoying getting into the Ghost band Mr. Gone and I can see many of the musical influences that shaped Tobias Forge as a performer and why he is still going strong after nearly twenty years. It's good that he isn't afraid to experiment with his band and not play it safe.</div> </div> </div> </div>Totally agree! I like how the band has some &quot;lore&quot; and how they change up the style a little bit with each iteration of &quot;Papa&quot;. Keeps thing a little fresh.<br /> <br /> I've liked all their albums so far, but the newer ones,. Impera and Skeleta, are high on the list right now. They're both really solid!<br /> <br /> Oh! And I forgot to say, but in Rite Here Rite Now, that live version of 'If you have Ghost' is amazing!! I loved how they played that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/\" target=\"_blank\">MrGone's Character Sheets</a><br /> For all your WoD Character Sheet Needs<br /> _________________________________<br /> Buy books &amp; pdfs from DTRPG and support my web site! <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=55414\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a><br /> Support my site on Patreon! <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mrgone\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24-mr-gone","name":"Mr Gone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-06-03T12:04:14-07:00","id":1551445,"title":"","content":"Papa Emeritus 3 and Cardinal Copia are my favorite frontmen. I am liking the current Papa V from the current album Mr. Gone and you still see Copia in the lore videos as Fater Imperator.<br /> <br /> In other things I have been enjoying that Games Workshop is putting out some more titles like the 3rd Legion from Warhammer 40K that are better known as the Emperor's Children and how they fell to Chaos and the hands of Slanish the God of Excess and Depravity.<br /> <br /> I hope at some point that Games Workshop will do a book on the Night Lords, World Eaters and Iron Warriors for Warhammer 40K at some point.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":27361,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","user":"Lysander","date":". 06-03-2025, 04:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-06-04T22:05:55-07:00","id":1551471,"title":"","content":"Speaking of Warhammer 40K it's good to see newer fans getting