s":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst","name":"Amethyst","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-06-27T08:23:47-07:00","id":1551882,"title":"","content":"I've finished Clair Obscur: Expedition 33 last weekend. Man, what a game! Just superb in terms of visuals, soundtrack, gameplay and voice-acting. I heard good things about it, so I bought it and went into it pretty much blind. Immediately I was surprised when I realised that the main-guy at the beginning was voiced by Charlie Cox (who plays Daredevil). And the premise/story hooked me within the first hour. It was one of those setups that throws a lot of information at you with the expectation that you'll be able to slowly figure out how it all fits together.<br /> <br /> Way too many narratives these days are too fearful to let the audience figure things out for themselves through context-clues and the like. This really reminded me of that recent <a href=\"https://www.nplusonemag.com/issue-49/essays/casual-viewing/\" target=\"_blank\">deep dive article on Netflix</a> where Will Tavlin wrote: <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Such slipshod filmmaking works for the streaming model, since audiences at home are often barely paying attention. Several screenwriters who\u2019ve worked for the streamer told me a common note from company executives is \u201chave this character announce what they\u2019re doing so that viewers who have this program on in the background can follow along.\u201d </div> </div> </div>These days it feels like 80% of storytelling in games, movies or TV shows works like that. So, it's refreshing to get a good story that isn't written with the assumption that you're an idiot. <br /> <br /> The way they handle combat in this game is also really interesting. Definitely my favorite game I've played so far this year.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-01T23:26:22-07:00","id":1551986,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iguazu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502231-feel-free-to-gush?p=1551868#post1551868\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I might look into Warhammer RPG; I found a copy of a Warhammer edition suspiciously cheap at a used-book store, that had the Vampire: Dark Ages books priced more than the original-cost. I suspect there are many, many versions of Warhammer out there.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh there is about 10 editions of the Warhammer 40 K game that will have contradictory lore and updated material from recent novels.<br /> <br /> For instance the most recent Dark Angels codex has updated lore on their recently returned Primarch Lionel Johnson and how he is dealing with a galaxy way different from what he knew from 10,000 years ago.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&qu