-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-10T15:49:28-07:00","id":1552276,"title":"","content":"Just finished the new Dungeons and Dragons 5th edition adventure anthology Dragon Delves. Loved it. Really happy I bought it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Amethyst is my birthstone. She/they.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst","name":"Amethyst","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-11T21:50:52-07:00","id":1552296,"title":"","content":"My attempt to paint my Warhammer 40 K Thousand Sons minis is going okay, but I still have lots to learn about painting on such small surfaces.<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/redface.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Embarrassment\" smilieid=\"2\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-13T10:12:20-07:00","id":1552334,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502231-feel-free-to-gush?p=1552174#post1552174\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Actually about the middle of the country.<br /> <br /> Only the far North of the country is in the Northern Hemisphere, and the idea that seasons don't exist in the tropics is a little exaggerated.<br /> <br /> I mean, where I live it's considered freezing cold when the temperature is about 15\u00ba C or below, and it won't get much lower than that. I've never personally seen snow in my life. Depending on many factors, this temperature remains during the whole day in the winter. In the summer here we can get as high as 36\u00ba C, so we're still talking about 20\u00ba of difference.<br /> <br /> There are places that vary considerably less, and others that vary considerably more, I'm not really near the Equator here. I'm from Bras\u00edlia.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've heard Brasilia has a comfortable-climate. I've lived in Buenos Aires; I got up north to Missiones, Iguazu, in October, and it was warm one day, and cold the next, but not Buenos Aires in August, cold. It was rather humid up there. I met a lot of Brazilians there because I spoke English and they don't want to speak Spanish and the ones from the southern parts of Brazil, near Uruguay, always said how cold it was on the coast of Southern-Brazil. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I have all the power in the world to give you, and all you have to do is beg&quot; -Nix<br /> <br /> &quot;There's thing about being a vampire, Frank; it takes a long fucking time to learn how do all the cool shit&quot;. -Abigail","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2521-iguazu","name":"Iguazu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2521_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"740"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-13T22:01:27-07:00","id":1552346,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iguazu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502231-feel-free-to-gush?p=1552334#post1552334\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I've heard Brasilia has a comfortable-climate. I've lived in Buenos Aires; I got up north to Missiones, Iguazu, in October, and it was warm one day, and cold the next, but not Buenos Aires in August, cold. It was rather humid up there. I met a lot of Brazilians there because I spoke English and they don't want to speak Spanish and the ones from the southern parts of Brazil, near Uruguay, always said how cold it was on the coast of Southern-Brazil.</div> </div> </div> </div>I love the climate around here. I've been to some of the cities known for actual hot climate, like Rio de Janeiro, and find it unbearable. Brasilia's warm days are already above my limit (although they only need an electric fan to deal with, at least where I live).<br /> <br /> Southern Brazil is actual temperate climate, and a lot of the region is mountainous, so it can get pretty cold there, enough for some places to see snow from time to time (and a very few to see it every year). It isn't terribly cold for someplace like Canada or northern Europe, but is still the same country of the rainforest, some hot deserts and savanas.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502231-feel-free-to-gush?p=1552296#post1552296\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My attempt to paint my Warhammer 40 K Thousand Sons minis is going okay, but I still have lots to learn about painting on such small surfaces.<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/redface.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Embarrassment\" smilieid=\"2\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>That's good to know! Post some photos if you feel like it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-24T16:10:06-07:00","id":1552638,"title":"","content":"I watched a really cool show on Netflix called Sirens. You guys should check it out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Amethyst is my birthstone. She/they.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst","name":"Amethyst","avatar":"https://forum.th