blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I recently picked up and watched Matt Reeves version of Batman and greatly appreciated the work of how film noir it looks and Robert Pattinson has come along way from his Twilight days.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I liked that one too. Although I do remember laughing when towards the end of the movie, somebody mentions in a serious tone that the Riddler &quot;has roughly 500 followers on social media&quot; <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> . That line always stuck with me. <br /> <br /> Have you seen the spin-off Penguin TV show where Colin Farrell reprises his role? That one's surprisingly good as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude00","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-21T14:12:41-07:00","id":1553348,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502231-feel-free-to-gush?p=1553330#post1553330\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I recently picked up and watched Matt Reeves version of Batman and greatly appreciated the work of how film noir it looks and Robert Pattinson has come along way from his Twilight days.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think I'll take a look at this.<br /> <br /> Robert Pattinson is a good actor, and was already a good actor in <i>Twilight</i>, regardless of the quality of the movie itself or the role. It's like Halle Berry in Catwoman, the problems of the movie simply had nothing to do with her acting. They both actually made good jobs in those respective roles, but that won't stop writing and direction from being bad. If the director says you meow, you meow.<br /> <br /> On another note: my wife is completely hooked on the game Dredge. She's been playing it for days on end.<br /> <br /> Which is great, except for the part where she has thalassophobia, nyctophobia, and overall a love hate with cosmic horror where she really fears it. So she has been staying awake all night and only sleeping when day breaks, because she can't sleep otherwise.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-23T05:58:06-07:00","id":1553396,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502231-feel-free-to-gush?p=1553344#post1553344\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, I liked that one too. Although I do remember laughing when towards the end of the movie, somebody mentions in a serious tone that the Riddler &quot;has roughly 500 followers on social media&quot; <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> . That line always stuck with me.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ha!! That cracked me up too! Can't decide if they thought that was a lot of what. LOL<br /> <br /> But the movie itself is pretty good! I need to rewatch it soon..<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502231-feel-free-to-gush?p=1553344#post1553344\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Have you seen the spin-off Penguin TV show where Colin Farrell reprises his role? That one's surprisingly good as well.</div> </div> </div> </div>I haven't yet, but I have it on disc, so I'm looking forward to seeing it!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/\" target=\"_blank\">MrGone's Character Sheets</a><br /> For all your WoD Character Sheet Needs<br /> _________________________________<br /> Buy books &amp; pdfs from DTRPG and support my web site! <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=55414\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a><br /> Support my site on Patreon! <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mrgone\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24-mr-gone","name":"Mr Gone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-23T14:31:23-07:00","id":1553410,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr Gone</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502231-feel-free-to-gush?p=1553396#post1553396\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ha!! That cracked me up too! Can't decide if they thought that was a lot of what. LOL</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, there are possibly two tropes at play here: the idea that the Riddler is a loser (he's usually perceived as such) and that the GCPD is severely incompetent.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude02","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-24T05:51:13-07:00","id":1553424,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502231-feel-free-to-gush?p=1553410#post1553410\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, there are possibly two tropes at play here: the idea that the Riddler is a loser (he's usually perceived as such) and that the GCPD is severely incompetent.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ha!! Yea, I think you nailed it! Which honestly makes that bit even funnier to me. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/\" target=\"_blank\">MrGone's Character Sheets</a><br /> For all your WoD Character Sheet Needs<br /> _________________________________<br /> Buy books &amp; pdfs from DTRPG and support my web site! <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=55414\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a><br /> Support my site on Patreon! <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mrgone\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24-mr-gone","name":"Mr Gone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-27T07:24:35-07:00","id":1553482,"title":"","content":"Since the second season of Peacemaker started airing, I went back and watched the first season. I heard it was good and yep, it really was that good. Honestly, the James Gunn humor got a bit grating later on in the season (maybe it would've worked better if I had watched it week to week as it was airing back then rather than multiple episodes at a time). It was only thanks to the series having a <i>great </i>cast that I didn't lose interest. The one that surprised me the most was Freddie Stroma as Adrian/Vigilante. I don't think I've seen him in other stuff I watched before recently. And I was surprised by John Cena. He was really filling out that role. Hard to imagine anyone else playing that role that way. He really gets the mix right between him being a do-gooder at heart while also being an oblivious airhead.<br /> <br /> The only thing that worries me a bit is that a friend who has already seen the first episode of the second season told me that the new season is gonna focus on the multiverse... sigh As much as I liked the first season... really, another multiverse-story? Maybe I gonna start watching Alien: Earth instead and watch that second season later...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-27T13:37:47-07:00","id":1553492,"title":"","content":"James Gunn has the problem/benefit of not following the actual comics lore in any way. His take is always wildly his, for better or worse. But yeah, I've heard good about John Cena's Peacemaker, he really made this iteration of the character.<br /> <br /> As for it being multiverse, I've been repeatedly bombarded with a trailer for the new season that straight up tells that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-27T19:45:03-07:00","id":1553503,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502231-feel-free-to-gush?p=1553492#post1553492\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> As for it being multiverse, I've been repeatedly bombarded with a trailer for the new season that straight up tells that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I didn't pay attention to those because I originally just thought &quot;You're finally gonna watch the first season and then you can continue right on with season 2 afterwards.&quot;. I mean, I don't even know if it's actually bad. It's just... there has been so much multiverse-stuff already with Marvel TV shows and movies and it's not gonna stop when they're gonna do the whole Jonathan Hickman Secret Wars thing with Avengers: Doomsday next year. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-30T08:46:42-07:00","id":1553553,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502231-feel-free-to-gush?p=1553482#post1553482\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Since the second season of Peacemaker started airing, I went back and watched the first season. I heard it was good and yep, it really was that good. Honestly, the James Gunn humor got a bit grating later on in the season (maybe it would've worked better if I had watched it week to week as it was airing back then rather than multiple episodes at a time). It was only thanks to the series having a <i>great </i>cast that I didn't lose interest. The one that surprised me the most was Freddie Stroma as Adrian/Vigilante. I don't think I've seen him in other stuff I watched before recently. And I was surprised by John Cena. He was really filling out that role. Hard to imagine anyone else playing that role that way. He really gets the mix right between him being a do-gooder at heart while also being an oblivious airhead.</div> </div> </div> </div>I absolutely loved the first season of Peacemaker! I thought they did a great job with that series, and I'm glad we're finally getting season 2, which started out pretty good I think.<br /> <br /> And I thought Vigilante was great! Freddie Stroma did an amazing job with that character! Next to John Cena, he's my second favorite of the show!<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/\" target=\"_blank\">MrGone's Character Sheets</a><br /> For all your WoD Character Sheet Needs<br /> _________________________________<br /> Buy books &amp; pdfs from DTRPG and support my web site! <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=55414\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a><br /> Support my site on Patreon! <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mrgone\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24-mr-gone","name":"Mr Gone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-09-02T09:06:47-07:00","id":1553588,"title":"","content":"I just finished reading In Memoriam. It was an amazing Vampire sourcebook. Really glad I bought it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Amethyst is my birthstone. She/they.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst","name":"Amethyst","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-09-02T09:10:51-07:00","id":1553589,"title":"","content":"A spot of potential good news on YouTube. It sounds like that Ranting For Vengeance might be losing his channel as the 15 year old teen has been reported enough for his racist, sexist, homophobic and antisemitic comments and the people in charge can no longer ignore it.<br /> \u200b<br /> I'll believe it when I see it as unfortunately hate and controversy sells. How I became aware of this teen was is that I'm a big fan of the Transformers and a few channels like Chris Mcfeely and Commdin Can who are big fans of the IP and I usually more likely to give there recommendations more serious weight were saying that Transformers One was a good film and not be put off by the trailer.<br /> <br /> So I watched the film and greatly enjoyed it and my only nitpicks was how it was marketed and how Shockwave was depicted as more emotional and prone to panic in high stress conditions.<br /> <br /> But this is an adaptation and details the origins the future Optimus Prime and Megatron and it's not going to be 100% faithful to the source material. Anyway Ranting For Vengeance showed up on my feed and I watched him and I was shocked by bad his take was and showed his ignorance of the lore.<br /> <br /> He didn't like the silly humor or scenes that was in it and showing he never watched the old G1 cartoon or even Beast Wars or in the old Marvel Comics or that we had absurd additions to the lore such as the Pretenders, Head, Target and Power Masters.<br /> <br /> But the worst thing was him going off was that the two voice actors who did Megatron and Bumblebee were Black and how much they sounded Black.<br /> <br /> That disturbed me as how does someone sound like a particular group and I didn't know or cared that the two actors had dark skin. All I cared about was that they did the roles well and they did.<br /> <br /> So afterwards I watched a few more videos of Ranting For Vengeance and saw that he wasn't ragebaiting or trolling at all and that he is a hateful person and I later found out that his Dad is worse and has his own channel called Red Pill MMA .<br /> <br /> Sorry for the long post.<br /> <br /> <br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":27361,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","user":"Lysander","date":". 09-03-2025, 03:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-09-02T21:58:10-07:00","id":1553602,"title":"","content":"On a happier note, I'll will be celebrating my 1 year anniversary at my current job and I still enjoy the work and I will get a raise and a better benefits package.<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-09-02T22:46:56-07:00","id":1553603,"title":"","content":"Found a neat channel on YouTube were they sing a lot of tolkien poetry and dwarven songs in general.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://youtube.com/@clamavideprofundis?si=RWdMCt0zQTDMS04N\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://youtube.com/@clamavideprofundis?si=RWdMCt0zQTDMS04N\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://youtube.com/@clamavideprofundis?si=RWdMCt0zQTDMS04N\" target=\"_blank\"> https://youtube.com/@clamavideprofundis?si=RWdMCt0zQTDMS04N </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://youtu.be/uxfoa23skHg?si=IfQ3E34oVanLYBJH\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://youtu.be/uxfoa23skHg?si=IfQ3E34oVanLYBJH\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://youtu.be/uxfoa23skHg?si=IfQ3E34oVanLYBJH\" target=\"_blank\"> https://youtu.be/uxfoa23skHg?si=IfQ3E34oVanLYBJH </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <br /> For some reason it really strikes an emotional nerve.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-09-04T17:24:14-07:00","id":1553627,"title":"","content":"Went to the doctor today and he thinks I may finally be at a point where I can safely take testosterone to help my transition but I do need to consult some specialists first.<br /> <br /> I've got another appointment scheduled six weeks from now and my husband and I are going to discuss it more in the meantime.<br /> <br /> Wish me luck!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm just a trans guy and gaming fan, unabashed hedonist and unusually upbeat nihilist, fairly laid back. He/Him.<br /> <br /> If everything is political, then nothing is!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25920-matt-corleone","name":"Matt Corleone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25920_8.webp","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-09-04T20:01:04-07:00","id":1553631,"title":"","content":"Good luck, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25920-matt-corleone\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar25920_8.webp');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"25920\" data-vbnamecard=\"25920\">Matt Corleone</a>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-09-04T22:18:18-07:00","id":1553634,"title":"","content":"I hope everything goes smoothly Matt Corleone.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-09-05T15:45:03-07:00","id":1553653,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr Gone</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502231-feel-free-to-gush?p=1553553#post1553553\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I absolutely loved the first season of Peacemaker! I thought they did a great job with that series, and I'm glad we're finally getting season 2, which started out pretty good I think.<br /> <br /> And I thought Vigilante was great! Freddie Stroma did an amazing job with that character! Next to John Cena, he's my second favorite of the show!<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Vigilante is great! Not only is Freddie Stroma great in that role but he matches John Cena's energy - while not simply copying him. Them hanging out in the woods just blowing shit up and having a laugh is so believable thanks to the actors.<br /> <br /> So what do you think of Season 2 thus far? Is it as good as the first season? Because as I mentioned before, I'm growing tired of the multiverse-stuff in these comic-stories.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-09-06T05:36:07-07:00","id":1553664,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502231-feel-free-to-gush?p=1553653#post1553653\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Vigilante is great! Not only is Freddie Stroma great in that role but he matches John Cena's energy - while not simply copying him. Them hanging out in the woods just blowing shit up and having a laugh is so believable thanks to the actors.</div> </div> </div> </div>Totally agree! I don't think I'd seen him in anything before, but he's definitely holding his own against John Cena! They're both so great in these roles!<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502231-feel-free-to-gush?p=1553653#post1553653\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So what do you think of Season 2 thus far? Is it as good as the first season? Because as I mentioned before, I'm growing tired of the multiverse-stuff in these comic-stories.</div> </div> </div> </div>I haven't seen the 3rd episode yet, but so far I'm really liking it! The multiverse stuff is ok, and at least they're doing it in an interesting way! <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"ma