post1554353\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I just finished watching 28 Years Later and it is a enjoyable film and they subverted expections with it not taking in the place of ruined cities but in the country side with survivors doing well as expected.</div> </div> </div> </div>I saw it a few weeks back and thought it was pretty good. Though it kind of goes off the rails in the last 5 minutes. LOL. But all in all, I thought it was a pretty nice follow up the other movies and I'll be looking forward to where they take it from there..","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/\" target=\"_blank\">MrGone's Character Sheets</a><br /> For all your WoD Character Sheet Needs<br /> _________________________________<br /> Buy books &amp; pdfs from DTRPG and support my web site! <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=55414\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a><br /> Support my site on Patreon! <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mrgone\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24-mr-gone","name":"Mr Gone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-17T02:53:38-07:00","id":1554406,"title":"","content":"Saw Paul Thomas Anderson's new movie &quot;One Battle After Another&quot; and had a great time with that one. Between this and Tarantino's &quot;Once Upon A Time In Hollywood&quot;, I think DiCaprio, it turns out, is actually pretty good at playing befuddled doofuses. Also, the casting for the Christmas-society was perfect. They did the &quot;bland, unremarkable middle-aged fascist white men&quot;-bit really well. Not just in terms of performances and writing but to the point where it was hard to tell the difference because of how similar they all looked. <br /> <br /> Also saw Tron: Ares. I really liked Tron and Tron: Legacy as a neat little sci-fi franchise that's more about style than substance. The Mike Bithell videogames (Tron - Identity and Tron - Catalyst) are a great addition to the franchise as well. But Tron: Ares... sigh. Well, the Nine Inch Nails soundtrack is great. That's a good thing at least. I still think the Daft Punk soundtrack for Tron: Legacy was better but this new Tron: Ares-one is definitely one of my favorite movie soundtracks for this year. But everything else... Honestly, the worst thing about the movie is the script. It's really bad. But not bad in a fun way. Just completely &quot;by-the-numbers, mind-numbingly boring&quot;-kind of bad. Although, to be fair, there was some great writing in the movie... when a character started directly quoting Mary Shelly's &quot;Frankenstein&quot;.<br /> <br /> And Jared Leto sucked. Also, it must be so annoying to make movies with this guy. He did the method-acting-thing again... for a goddamn Tron-movie! Like, he expected people to call him &quot;Ares&quot; (like his movie character) even when the camera's weren't rolling. Hopefully, between this and Morbius, this will cause Jared Leto to do some self-reflection. Because his whole &quot;process&quot; doesn't even lead to him giving great performances...<br /> <br /> I played through Hades 2, Supergiant Games' new release and it was great. It's a sequel in the best possible way: It's everything that mades Hades great - except there's even more, new stuff added to it. Also, really love how music has become more and more important to the games of this developer. The soundtrack is amazing and at this point, I feel like it would be fitting if their next game would just be a full-blown musical. There are so many great musical moments in this game. But as a rogue-lite the game's also super-fun and polished. Once again, they just took stuff from the first game and just added even more variety and complexity to it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-17T04:59:37-07:00","id":1554415,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502231-feel-free-to-gush?p=1554263#post1554263\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I never heard of the Steel Dragons, I know that the Silver Dragons would assume a human looking form to visit civilization.</div> </div> </div> </div>Chromatic dragons, Metallic dragons, Gem dragons, Steel dragons, Ferrous dragons, Lung dragons, not to say a number of particular species that don't belong to a family, like Abyssal, Rainbow, Pink, Force, Solar, Moon, Brown, Deep, Fang, the list goes on.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"http