ount":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-23T15:40:06-07:00","id":1554616,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502231-feel-free-to-gush?p=1554606#post1554606\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mission Impossible Dead Reckoning is a great movie and excellent ending to the series and seeing some of the callbacks to previous films was a good idea to tie things all together.</div> </div> </div> </div>(I think you mean &quot;Final Reckoning&quot; (aka &quot;Dead Reckoning Part 2&quot;)... yeah, the titles of these movies got a bit confusing at the end there<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />)<br /> <br /> Usually, I would cringe at that but bringing back the computer guy from the first Mission Impossible was one of the best parts of the movie. Rolf Saxon was such a delight in this movie. That was a great performance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-23T19:25:00-07:00","id":1554630,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502231-feel-free-to-gush?p=1554606#post1554606\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mission Impossible Dead Reckoning is a great movie and excellent ending to the series and seeing some of the callbacks to previous films was a good idea to tie things all together.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Ending&quot; until the next installment, as the <i>Mission: Impossible</i> movie franchise is already the second revival of the original series. And Tom Cruise is already talking about maybe doing new movies in the future.<br /> <br /> But I don't watch Cruise's movies to begin with, given the horrible person he is, the horrible things he do and the horrible organization he represents.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-24T13:19:12-07:00","id":1554647,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502231-feel-free-to-gush?p=1554630#post1554630\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> &quot;Ending&quot; until the next installment, as the <i>Mission: Impossible</i> movie franchise is already the second revival of the original series. And Tom Cruise is already talking about maybe doing new movies in the future.<br /> <br /> But I don't watch Cruise's movies to begin with, given the horrible person he is, the horrible things he do and the horrible organization he represents.</div> </div> </div> </div>Personally, I'd prefer it to just end. But who knows... The only thing I wish won't happen is that we're gonna get some sort of reboot or Tom Cruise as a &quot;mentor figure&quot; in a sequel. Then again, I wouldn't be surprised if that were to happen, either... Hollywood loves their franchises these days... sigh <br /> <br /> As for Tom Cruise... Kinda remarkable how he managed to rebrand himself after the Oprah-couch-thing. If anything, I think he should want another Mission Impossible movie. Because I always think Tom Cruise will become a saint if he accidentally dies during one of those practical Mission Impossible stunts. Imagine the coverage... and I can easily imagine people getting angry if you bring up Scientology in that context. His whole history will get sanitized if that were to happen, I think.<br /> <br /> As for unwatchable... personally, I have a bigger issue with seeing Kevin Spacey and Woody Allen. They were in some pretty good movies back in the day but hell, every time I see them when switching TV channels... I mean, Kevin Spacey is the worst one. Now looking back on it, the bad vibes weren't a result of acting, it feels like and more just Kevin Spacey being Kevin Spacey.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-24T21:57:44-07:00","id":1554658,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502231-feel-free-to-gush?p=1554647#post1554647\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Personally, I'd prefer it to just end. But who knows... The only thing I wish won't happen is that we're gonna get some sort of reboot or Tom Cruise as a &quot;mentor figure&quot; in a sequel. Then again, I wouldn't be surprised if that were to happen, either... Hollywood loves their franchises these days... sigh<br /> <br /> As for Tom Cruise... Kinda remarkable how he managed to rebrand himself after the Oprah-couch-thing. If anything, I think he should want another Mission Impossible movie. Because I always think Tom Cruise will become a saint if he accidentally dies during one of those practical Mission Impossible stunts. Imagine the coverage... and I can easily imagine people getting angry if you bring up Scientology in that context. His whole history will get sanitized if that were to happen, I think.<br /> <br /> As for unwatchable... personally, I have a bigger issue with seeing Kevin Spacey and Woody Allen. They were in some pretty good movies back in the day but hell, every time I see them when switching TV channels... I mean, Kevin Spacey is the worst one. Now looking back on it, the bad vibes weren't a result of acting, it feels like and more just Kevin Spacey being Kevin Spacey.</div> </div> </div> </div>Here's the thing for MI, Cruise's character isn't really what makes the franchise. It's not about Ethan, but about the IMF itself. Oh, and of course, about the theme music, that things survived unabated for 3 decades in popular culture without anything to ground it. Everyone knew the MI theme at a time most people had never seen MI, and that was all over the world.<br /> <br /> So a reboot isn't necessary. It may happen, but would be a stupid decision. Ethan as a mentor figure... that's more likely with Cruise's apparent wish to eventually come back to the role.<br /> <br /> On not watching him, that's a complex issue, and I'll start of stating that I don't think in any way my take is definitive, not even for myself. But Cruise's actions are a problem for me because he uses his money and influence to forward Scientology's power, and that means doing harm in whole another scale compared to a &quot;personal criminal&quot;. There are three things that make it worse for me: the harm done is socially more significant, it is tied to the work itself, and on watching it I'm financing or otherwise contributing to it somehow.<br /> <br /> That's why, as an example, I prefer to read Samurai X (whose mangaka was arrested for keeping child porn, disgusting man) than Harry Potter (whose author isn't just extremely vocal against trans rights and trans in general, but also finances anti-trans works).<br /> <br /> I also think in general that work is too much of a fundamental right, that it shouldn't be attacked unless it's the very means of the crime. Spacey, and to a greater extent Whedon, used the acess and money they got from their work to do what they did, that's worth boycotting if justice isn't reaching them otherwise. Allen apparently did his evil in domestic context only, which is certainly a horrible thing, but also means boycotting his work wouldn't affect anything.<br /> <br /> Also, whenever justice can be served in a more adequate way, it should. Allen, Spacey, Whedon and many others should face prison time. Anything less than that is avoiding the real problem. Cruise has the problem that he didn't commit any crime (except being complicit with sex slavery for himself, but the crime is more by the Scientology than himself and can't currently be proved), he just support an extremely reprehensible organization, even if one that should, by all means, be outlawed and properly investigated.<br /> <br /> But again, while my overall premises are those, this is a rather complex subject. If you can't stand an artist, that's it. If you can't be away from an artist, that's it, too. And a detail on Watsuki's case: the problem is more the Japanese law than him being let go. He was found guilty, but in Japan his crime is met with a fine, since he wasn't linked to the production of the material. There are signs that the investigation was interrupted too soon, so they never found out how he got it, but that's not on him exactly. He paid 200.000 yen, which was about 1.900 USD at the time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-29T06:25:15-07:00","id":1554767,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502231-feel-free-to-gush?p=1554658#post1554658\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Here's the thing for MI, Cruise's character isn't really what makes the franchise. It's not about Ethan, but about the IMF itself. Oh, and of course, about the theme music, that things survived unabated for 3 decades in popular culture without anything to ground it. Everyone knew the MI theme at a time most people had never seen MI, and that was all over the world.<br /> <br /> So a reboot isn't necessary. It may happen, but would be a stupid decision. Ethan as a mentor figure... that's more likely with Cruise's apparent wish to eventually come back to the role.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm, I wonder how many people even still remember that Mission Impossible was originally based on a TV show. <br /> <br /> I remember that at one point, they were thinking of taking Rebecca Ferguson's character Ilsa Faust and make her a successor. But then they killed her off because Rebecca Ferguson wanted out because the shoots for these MI-movies were getting too long for her.<br /> <br /> I mean, that's the other thing with these movies: The shoots are usually VERY long. Understandable, of course. They're shooting on location internationally, action-set-pieces... That takes time. And then they usually go over-budget with these movies as well. That's why I'm wondering if they even would still want a potential next MI-movie to still be produced in this manner if Tom Cruise isn't attached to it. That's why a reboot could make sense. You still cash in on the name of the franchise but you scale back the production, get some new actors (who cost less than Tom Cruise) and hopefully, people are interested going to the cinema for this. Well, I guess, you could also forgo the cinema-part and partner up with Netflix, save some more money by having Netflix pitch in and just release it for streaming. Will it be a good movie? Doubtful. But I could picture something like this happening, if they want to wring some money out of this franchise even without Tom Cruise attached to it.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502231-feel-free-to-gush?p=1554658#post1554658\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On not watching him, that's a complex issue, and I'll start of stating that I don't think in any way my take is definitive, not even for myself. But Cruise's actions are a problem for me because he uses his money and influence to forward Scientology's power, and that means doing harm in whole another scale compared to a &quot;personal criminal&quot;. There are three things that make it worse for me: the harm done is socially more significant, it is tied to the work itself, and on watching it I'm financing or otherwise contributing to it somehow.<br /> <br /> That's why, as an example, I prefer to read Samurai X (whose mangaka was arrested for keeping child porn, disgusting man) than Harry Potter (whose author isn't just extremely vocal against trans rights and trans in general, but also finances anti-trans works).<br /> <br /> I also think in general that work is too much of a fundamental right, that it shouldn't be attacked unless it's the very means of the crime. Spacey, and to a greater extent Whedon, used the acess and money they got from their work to do what they did, that's worth boycotting if justice isn't reaching them otherwise. Allen apparently did his evil in domestic context only, which is certainly a horrible thing, but also means boycotting his work wouldn't affect anything.<br /> <br /> Also, whenever justice can be served in a more adequate way, it should. Allen, Spacey, Whedon and many others should face prison time. Anything less than that is avoiding the real problem. Cruise has the problem that he didn't commit any crime (except being complicit with sex slavery for himself, but the crime is more by the Scientology than himself and can't currently be proved), he just support an extremely reprehensible organization, even if one that should, by all means, be outlawed and properly investigated.<br /> <br /> But again, while my overall premises are those, this is a rather complex subject. If you can't stand an artist, that's it. If you can't be away from an artist, that's it, too. And a detail on Watsuki's case: the problem is more the Japanese law than him being let go. He was found guilty, but in Japan his crime is met with a fine, since he wasn't linked to the production of the material. There are signs that the investigation was interrupted too soon, so they never found out how he got it, but that's not on him exactly. He paid 200.000 yen, which was about 1.900 USD at the time.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I think I'm with you on this. Ultimately, everybody has to draw the line for themselves when it comes to the whole &quot;separating the art from the artist&quot;-convo. But it also should never be forgotten why some people will want to avoid particular artists.<br /> <br /> Allen, Spacey, Whedon... Bryan Singer is another one I would add to that list. It's insane how after all their bad behavior has become public knowledge, you then often hear how for the people in the industry, it was more like an open secret that these people were predatory and/or awful to be around. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-29T14:46:31-07:00","id":1554795,"title":"","content":"I picked up one of the old Marve Comicsl Transformers Omnibus that focused on the last 50 or so issues of there run along with the attempt with Generation 2 and Transformers The Movie comic. It's amazing how much the characters looks have changed with the passage of time and how the artwork is so different. I should mention that it's always been strange how the characters don't always match how they looked in the cartoon such as Megatron and Galvatron or Optimus Prime. <br /> <br /> I still liked the series and it holds up pretty good from when I first picked it up as preteen.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-29T20:27:26-07:00","id":1554816,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502231-feel-free-to-gush?p=1554767#post1554767\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmm, I wonder how many people even still remember that Mission Impossible was originally based on a TV show.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a good point, and it will certainly influence their decision. The franchised isn't attached to Cruise, but he really became its face for the public in the 21st century.<br /> <br /> But then, once he's not an option anymore, reminding the public through a marketing campaign about the old times is a solid option.<br /> <br /> A mere continuation isn't just possible, it has the same benefits of a reboot, hence I think it would be a stupid decision to reboot it (i.e. make a version where the other movies didn't happened).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502231-feel-free-to-gush?p=1554767#post1554767\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean, that's the other thing with these movies: The shoots are usually VERY long. Understandable, of course. They're shooting on location internationally, action-set-pieces... That takes time. And then they usually go over-budget with these movies as well.</div> </div> </div> </div>Add to that that they don't necessarily make wonders for an actor's career.<br /> <br /> Making Action Movies is hard, but is still seen in the Academy as an inferior work. Some artists can get away with it for one reason or another, but most who want to rise and get better roles (and payment) will sooner or later have to ditch it at least for a time for other kinds of work, if they have the opportunity.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502231-feel-free-to-gush?p=1554767#post1554767\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, I guess, you could also forgo the cinema-part and partner up with Netflix, save some more money by having Netflix pitch in and just release it for streaming. Will it be a good movie? Doubtful. But I could picture something like this happening, if they want to wring some money out of this franchise even without Tom Cruise attached to it.</div> </div> </div> </div>They may even go back to the origins and make a series.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502231-feel-free-to-gush?p=1554767#post1554767\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, I think I'm with you on this. Ultimately, everybody has to draw the line for themselves when it comes to the whole &quot;separating the art from the artist&quot;-convo. But it also should never be forgotten why some people will want to avoid particular artists.</div> </div> </div> </div>We should always be aware of who the artists are, and if they do wrong, hold them accountable, regardless if this will become a boycott or not.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502231-feel-free-to-gush?p=1554767#post1554767\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Allen, Spacey, Whedon... Bryan Singer is another one I would add to that list. It's insane how after all their bad behavior has become public knowledge, you then often hear how for the people in the industry, it was more like an open secret that these people were predatory and/or awful to be around.</div> </div> </div> </div>Unfortunately that's the industry for you. And not only the movies industry, but every industry.<br /> <br /> Rich and/or successful people regularly get away with a lot of things, and yes, those are frequently open secrets. I work at a big bank and I hear a lot of stories both within the company, the industry in general and among our corporate clients.<br /> <br /> It's terrible, and very little anyone can do most of the time, because the accountability systems we have as a society are built to protect the perpetrator unless you either have overwhelming evidence or the most vulnerable and resourceless people involved, the victims themselves, do a lot of the legwork themselves.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502231-feel-free-to-gush?p=1554795#post1554795\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I picked up one of the old Marve Comicsl Transformers Omnibus that focused on the last 50 or so issues of there run along with the attempt with Generation 2 and Transformers The Movie comic. It's amazing how much the characters looks have changed with the passage of time and how the artwork is so different. I should mention that it's always been strange how the characters don't always match how they looked in the cartoon such as Megatron and Galvatron or Optimus Prime.</div> </div> </div> </div>I started on Transformers when I was a kid, with Brazilian reruns of the first series. And to be honest I kind of left at that.<br /> <br /> <br /> On another note, I'm currently watching <i>Sandman</i>, as many people told me to do. It's quite different from the comics, but very good nonetheless.<br /> <br /> And of course, it plays on what I said earlier about knowing your artists. I won't join Gaiman's cancellation, first because I must recognize I love his works too much, second because his crimes have nothing to do with his work, and third he's already being held accountable, lets see how far the whole thing goes. Oh, and fourth, usually I don't join those things when all we have are fresh accusations without evidence. We have to take the victims seriously and help them, but that doesn't mean someone is guilty by default.<br /> <br /> We already had cases where the artist saying the accusations are lies were, indeed, telling the truth. And others where the truth was far more complex and weird (like with Johnny Depp).\u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-01T13:36:52-07:00","id":1554918,"title":"","content":"I enjoyed that IDW did take risks with the Transformers universe and moved the story along with both the Autobots &amp; Decepticons coming to tense cease fire and trying to get over eons of mistrust and seeing that many of the folks on both sides of the conflict realized how much they have been changed and couldn't go back to their old lives. On the Neil Gaiman front and I won't stop enjoying his work on Sandman and American Gods novel.<br /> <br /> The same thing with Charlie Sheen and his substance abuse issues and I'm not inclined to buy Corey Feldman's allegations that Sheen sexually assaulted the late Corey Haim on the set of Lucas.<br /> <br /> Feldman has his own issues about creditabilty and he always struck me as someone always trying to keep himself in the public eye as his movie career stalled. and I'm more inclined to believe Haim's Mother and Sister saying it wasn't Sheen that did the deed , but one of Feldman's now dead friends . But this should be on a vent thread.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-01T19:32:41-07:00","id":1554927,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502231-feel-free-to-gush?p=1554918#post1554918\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The same thing with Charlie Sheen and his substance abuse issues</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't blame people for substance abuses to begin with, I find the whole depiction of them as immoral as abhorrent.<br /> <br /> People who abuse substances are sick. They need help, not boycott. Even if this makes them horrible to live around, there's a huge difference between recognizing they're not in shape to work and blaming them on being like that, and the later only worsens the situation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-02T01:13:06-07:00","id":1554947,"title":"","content":"Charlie Sheen admitted that he was in no shape to do Anger Management in recent interviews.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-02T23:42:24-08:00","id":1555003,"title":"","content":"By the way, what I said earlier also counts for people in your life.<br /> <br /> If a loved one deals with addiction, be it to a substance or anything, really, know their ability to resist is <b>severely</b> impaired. It's not lack of willpower, resilience, love or responsibility. They're sick. They will do bad things and lash out when denied their fix, but it's not because they don't care. Expecting them to do otherwise is both unwise and unfair, blaming them is outright cruel.<br /> <br /> This doesn't mean you should stick to those people at any cost, their addiction may become a burden you simply can't carry, too. But they need help, and they need your love more than ever.<br /> <br /> Addiction isn't only for drugs, either. People may get addicted to anything, literally. The pathways in the brain are the very same, whether it's cocaine, gambling or praying. I've seen some shit with people addicted to all kinds of things. Substance abuse get the additional problem of substance dependence, it's <b>not</b> the same. The most striking cases usually have both, but people may have only addiction or only dependence. They also need to be treated separately.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-03T13:18:35-08:00","id":1555035,"title":"","content":"This week is going well. Heroes of Faerun has been pretty good so far, Adventures in Faerun looks good too, and I\u2019m looking forward to the next release for Trinity Continuum.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Amethyst is my birthstone. She/they.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst","name":"Amethyst","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-04T10:55:53-08:00","id":1555062,"title":"","content":"It's always a good day when Space Ice uploads a objectively bad film and roasts it and especially when it is a Seagal film and you wonder how many more bad films did Steven Seagal make. If Space Ice runs out of Seagal films there's always films from the Rock.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-04T16:45:39-08:00","id":1555080,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502231-feel-free-to-gush?p=1555062#post1555062\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">how many more bad films did Steven Seagal make.</div> </div> </div> </div>A little more than 50.<br /> <br /> He has about 4 or 5 good movies, although it must be made clear that they're not good because of him.<br /> <br /> Dude manages to be worse than Jean Claude Van Damme, who's worse than the Rock ever was. Although it must be said, Van Damme has a disposition to follow others' ideas and do humble roles that kind of compensate in his filmography (although he'll never be forgiven for <i>Street Fighter</i>). The Rock and Vin Diesel have both a lot of the problems that kept Seagal doing bad movies.<br /> <br /> If you want someone with an actual good filmography and acting skills among the Action Muscle Crew, you want Arnold Schwarzenegger. Despite his inability to hide the accent, he's just good at what he does, and he does far more than the others, both in Action and Comedy movies.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-04T21:47:12-08:00","id":1555090,"title":"","content":"I always liked Jean Claude Van Damme in spite of his limited acting range and you could see the natural charm he had to aid him. I've seen his more recent films and he has improved his acting range. Space Ice loves Jean Claude Van Damme films along with Nicholas Cage, Arnold Schwarzenegger and Stallone with the over the top actions.<br /> <br /> He likes to make fun of Seagal for the bad acting, over use of body and audio doubles and how he can't even bothered to try to make an effort to be better in his films. <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-05T01:25:09-08:00","id":1555100,"title":"","content":"Yeah, acting skills are important, but there are a lot of other attitudes that can make or break your role in a movie.<br /> <br /> Van Damme is bad, but he doesn't shy from whatever the movie requires from him. Even his worst scene, the <i>Street Fighter</i> speech, was mostly the fault of whomever wrote it, and you can say the director should have just cut it or put another character to do it. It had no reason to happen except American Exceptionalism. He was perfect in <i>Universal Soldier</i>, as it was a mix of a story almost tailor-made for his lack of acting skills and his willingness to be what the movie needs, even if it is someone vulnerable and scarred.<br /> <br /> Seagal is terrible to work with. He only accepts very similar roles, overly badass veterans of half a dozen government agencies that never die. He already threatened to sue a director that refused to make an extra scene in a movie for his character to survive. Even apart all the dubious shit in his life, he's an asshole to work with, and that only limits him. And he simply thinks his skill with martial arts make him perfect at what he does. Good movies with him happen sometimes because some directors know how to use him as he is, and not a bit more.<br /> <br /> Rock and Diesel both have better acting skills than the old crew could get away with in the 80s and 90s, but they also have a lot of the smug attitude of Seagal. They also want Schwarzenegger's fame, and that's horrible because they try to do things they're not really good at. They have other strong suits than basic muscle-action, but comedy isn't one of those.<br /> <br /> AFAIK Stallone is pretty good, especially taking into account that his expression and speech are literally physically impaired. But he's actually even more accomplished as writer and director, as he wrote most of his films. Overall he's a more complete artist, so to speak, and that has an effect on his acting as most of his movies are literally tailor-made for him. And yes, he wrote or co-wrote every single <i>Rocky</i> and <i>Rambo</i> movie.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-05T13:21:18-08:00","id":1555134,"title":"","content":"Oh I agree that a great attitude also helps in the working environment and from what I heard of Segal is that he is a real rotten person. <br /> <br /> Then you have guys like Keanu Reeves who despite a limited acting range is well liked and people enjoy working with him.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-05T21:14:28-08:00","id":1555153,"title":"","content":"On other note I have recently been listening to songs from Halestorm latest album and I am pleased by how good they sound.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-08T12:21:19-08:00","id":1555244,"title":"","content":"Saw &quot;Predator: Badlands&quot; and it was way better than I expected. To be honest, the idea of making a Predator-movie where the Predator is the protagonist seemed a bit dubious to me but this movie works surprisingly well. The best part about it is that it's just fun. Especially in the second half when it becomes clear what the movie is really about. It's pretty light on story and character but it's all pretty straightforward. The thing that still makes it entertaining despite that is the action-scenes. They are actually quite good and well-choreographed. The movie's also pretty good in the design of the alien flora and fauna. This is the kind of movie I wish Tron: Ares had been. Just a really fun sci-fi-action-movie. <br /> <br /> Also saw Kathryn Bigelow's new movie &quot;House Of Dynamite&quot;... Let's just say towards the end of the movie the US-president actually says &quot;I've heard on a podcast once that our world is like a house of dynamite.&quot; - and this is supposed to be a profound moment. That gave me a good laugh. And others in the theater were laughing too. So, that was a good moment. To describe the movie a little bit: It's a very detail-oriented, realistic movie about the US-government-response to a nuclear warhead that's headed for the US. It's very realistic. It's also one of the most empty-headed movies I've seen in a while. Like, think about the premise. Would it shock you to imagine people being stressed about it or people worrying about loved ones? Yep, that's in the movie. And that's it. The movie has nothing else to say about the topic. Seriously. The last minute of Christopher Nolan's Oppenheimer had more to say about nuclear weapons than this two hour movie. That certainly was an interesting experience.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-08T19:00:25-08:00","id":1555255,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div cl