zu","name":"Iguazu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2521_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"740"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-10T15:03:06-08:00","id":1555333,"title":"","content":"I saw a teaser trailer for the upcoming Wolverine game and it looks very good and should be a big seller if the game play mechanics are sound. I wonder if they will include Kitty Pryde, and Mystique in the game along with Jean Grey as the have strong connections to the Wolverine lore?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":27361,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","user":"Lysander","date":". 11-10-2025, 06:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-11T04:08:11-08:00","id":1555357,"title":"","content":"Things to gush about<b></b>: we\u2019re starting a new Trinity Continuum campaign this week for the first time in a couple years, so I\u2019m happy about that. Also, I\u2019m really excited for the final season of Stranger Things, which is coming out in a little more than two weeks.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Amethyst is my birthstone. She/they.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude00","count":1},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst","name":"Amethyst","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-14T05:12:34-08:00","id":1555471,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502231-feel-free-to-gush?p=1555333#post1555333\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I saw a teaser trailer for the upcoming Wolverine game and it looks very good and should be a big seller if the game play mechanics are sound. I wonder if they will include Kitty Pryde, and Mystique in the game along with Jean Grey as the have strong connections to the Wolverine lore?</div> </div> </div> </div>I have high hopes for that Wolverine game! The Spider-Man games were really good, so hopefully they can make this one just as good. And I used to be a HUGE Wolverine fan, so if they dig into the lore and include some of those characters that'd be amazing!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/\" target=\"_blank\">MrGone's Character Sheets</a><br /> For all your WoD Character Sheet Needs<br /> _________________________________<br /> Buy books &amp; pdfs from DTRPG and support my web site! <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=55414\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a><br /> Support my site on Patreon! <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mrgone\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24-mr-gone","name":"Mr Gone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-16T09:32:52-08:00","id":1555500,"title":"","content":"Finished Outer Worlds 2. It was pretty good and I liked it more than the first one. Also liked it more than Obsidian's other game, their attempt at a Skyrim-esque game Avowed (still can't believe they decided to force you to play a god-touched). It's a pretty good sequel in the sense that it has improved stuff from the first game, especially when it comes the game's skill-system and the flaw-system. But having finished it, I feel like some skills are more worthwhile than others (putting points in Speech felt more like a must than an option, for example). The option to go third-person this time around felt nice but the sneak-animations looked just silly. Maybe they will fix that later. The story was... okay. At the end, it does come off like one of those stories that could've been solved immediately if everybody had just talked to each other.<br /> <br /> But I did love the addition of the radio-channels. Lots of creativity there. Each of the three main-factions has a radio-channel and some of the best writing, in my opinion, was right there. And the music was also great. The math-obsessed Order making a song about how great prime-numbers are and the capitalist Auntie's Choice channel's promoting a musical about how the company got founded, for example. Stuff like that. Definitely had a good time. I wouldn't put it on my GOTY-list but it was pretty good.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-16T11:07:53-08:00","id":1555502,"title":"","content":"I'm not playing it now, but have fond memories already of <i>Catherine Full Body</i>. So many interesting details packed in such a short story. The framing device is kinda clich\u00e9 despite uncommon in a game, but it works. Even noticing that Catherine is full of BS from the get-go, watching Vincent's confusion and how he deals with it is so much fun.<br /> <br /> My only complaint is with Qatherine disappearing mid-game if you don't follow the correct route. I know it's extra content, but it would have been fun if the game were further adapted.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-19T23:11:41-08:00","id":1555672,"title":"","content":"I picked up some newer Cyberforce stuff from Top Cow part of Image. I must say that I enjoyed the concept of cybernetic superheroes or anti heroes in this case.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.co