\"https://www.patreon.com/mrgone\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24-mr-gone","name":"Mr Gone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-01T23:52:55-08:00","id":1556085,"title":"","content":"I recently picked up Transformers Volume 4 by Image Comics and they are still delivering to me engaging stories. <br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b<br /> Some minor spoilers are about Megatron being kidnapped by the Quintessons and forced to endure cruel and violent tests in the past and getting more and more violent and cruel as a result and how he got a third alternate mode that gave him a degree of mental control over his followers.<br /> <br /> We learn that Astrotrain hatred for Megatron stems from the loss of a loved one at the leaders hand. All in all I have enjoyed this take on the Transformers and seeing how Prime leads and Megatron terrorizing his army to follow him.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-02T04:41:02-08:00","id":1556092,"title":"","content":"The first four episodes of the Stranger Things final season are amazing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Amethyst is my birthstone. She/they.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst","name":"Amethyst","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-02T21:57:23-08:00","id":1556114,"title":"","content":"I really enjoyed Matt Reeves Batman and Rian Johnson Glass Onion. RIan Johnson proved that he is still a great filmmaker despite his rather awful Star Wars movie from a few years back. Even the best creatives can have flops.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-03T00:46:17-08:00","id":1556118,"title":"","content":"His Star Wars film wasn't really a flop even if it was divisive among fans. It crossed the billion dollar mark in ticket sales, so a lot of people went to see it, and the reviews are more positive than not. It is however, much better seeing him doing films that clearly suit him much better than that though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-03T11:26:39-08:00","id":1556127,"title":"","content":"I should have phrased it better Heavy Arms about Rian Johnson Star Wars movie impact on the fandom and how polarized it made things. I always felt that he was a good director from his days on the Bruce Willis movie Looper.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-03T14:54:14-08:00","id":1556138,"title":"","content":"We have a certain tendency to value every work of art through the lenses of qualitative criticism: if we liked it, and if the people talking about it are talking good things.<br /> <br /> But there are many ways to evaluate art depending on its purposes and circumstances, and sometimes we're just too blind to how some people do not really seek the quality standards we want.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-04T12:41:19-08:00","id":1556152,"title":"","content":"On a lark, I decided to watch the direct to dvd/Blu Ray movie Fight or Flight with Joss Hartnett and Katie Sackoff (spelling?), and I found it a nice fun movie that the people knew it for it was.<br /> <br /> Just simple fun escapism fantasy and you can't go wrong with that.<br /> <br /> On a side note I have been watching videos about possibly austim coded characters in popular culture and how well or poorly portrayed they are. I find it interesting but I'm no doctor as my psychiatrist knowledge begins and ends with Jonathan Kellerman Alex Delaware series and he has a background in that field.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":27361,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","user":"Lysander","date":". 12-04-2025, 03:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-04T14:54:46-08:00","id":1556155,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502231-feel-free-to-gush?p=1556152#post1556152\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On a side note I have been watching videos about possibly austim coded characters in popular culture and how well or poorly portrayed they are. I find it interesting but I'm no doctor as my psychiatrist knowledge begins and ends with Jonathan Kellerman Alex Delaware series and he has a background in that field.</div> </div> </div> </div>Jonathan Kellerman is a Psychologist, not a Psychiatrist, so that's telling.<br /> <br /> The problem with &quot;Autism Coded&quot; characters is that there's no such a thing, this is wishful thinking.<br /> <br /> Coded characters are a subversion, they're an unspoken but purposefully designed reference. Characters with autistic-like traits are not meant to be a reference. Their traits do come from a lot of Neurodiversity in human history, but not from an understanding of those people as &quot;Autistic&quot; or something like that.<br /> <br /> Autistic characters are a relatively recent phenomenon, but they're identified as Autistic.<br /> <br /> Particularly, &quot;autistic-coded&quot; characters are, more often than not, by people who don't have a strong conceptualization of what Autism is, or any whatsoever, they wouldn't even recognize their characters as Autistic. Character-coding has to do with making either veiled representation or veiled statements about a group, &quot;autistic-coded&quot; are born from the group not even being recognized as such.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-04T16:45:31-08:00","id":1556158,"title":"","content":"So in other words, it's deceptive language <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-04T16:59:39-08:00","id":1556160,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502231-feel-free-to-gush?p=1556158#post1556158\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So in other words, it's deceptive language</div> </div> </div> </div>An actual coded character, yes, in a sense.<br /> <br /> Queer-coded characters are a prime example, some are means for queer artists to put representation in a work they're not allowed to put an openly Queer character on. Others are means for bigot ones to attribute other characteristics to LGBTQIAP+ people without calling them out directly. Many are a sum of both as they're the work of many hands, Disney is full of those, for example.<br /> <br /> Jew-coded characters are all over the place, reinforcing racist tropes and conspiracy theories, as are to a lesser degree coded characters for other ethnicities and religions.<br /> <br /> But I wouldn't say the people looking for Autistic-coded characters is engaging in deceptive language, I think they're just confused as they want to find representation in already existing works. It's a sentiment I know very well, but the reality is that Autism simply wasn't well known and most of those characteristics used to identify &quot;Autistic-coded characters&quot; weren't associated with Autism, regardless if they are or not common in Autistics.<br /> <br /> Without purposefully association, there's no character-coding.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-04T17:45:10-08:00","id":1556161,"title":"","content":"I can see your point Monteparnas and I know some will use it as a catch all phrase when describing certain characters.<br /> <br /> In Warhammer 40 K I have heard rather dismissively that Lion El Jonson who is the Primarch of the Dark Angels being labeled that as he isn't the most friendly or social of the Emperor's sons.<br /> <br /> It couldn't possibly be that he spent his formative years avoiding and hunting the chaos warped beasts of Caliban and making any noise meant the difference between life and death and when Luther found him and taught him human society that he still remained blunt and was more of actions mean more then words type.<br /> <br /> In fact in later deciptions he is trying to be more understanding and empathetic to other people needs.<br /> <br /> Or Sherlock Holmes being viewed as being on the spectrum, when he could be just is a jerk who battles depression and drug addiction.<br /> <br /> On a totally different and fun note. The YouTuber Multiversial Wisdom who uses Batman as his primary character to react to other properties or containment plans for people who he may encounter. He did a reaction to Vampire the Masquerade setting and it was pretty good.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":27361,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","user":"Lysander","date":". 12-05-2025, 12:52 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-06T19:59:42-08:00","id":1556278,"title":"","content":"I'm interested in seeing Predator Badlands as I'm interested in seeing a film that is viewed from the Predator's POV as it hasn't been done before in the movie series.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-12T04:23:34-08:00","id":1556512,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502231-feel-free-to-gush?p=1556278#post1556278\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm interested in seeing Predator Badlands as I'm interested in seeing a film that is viewed from the Predator's POV as it hasn't been done before in the movie series.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yea, I'm pretty excited to see it too! Looks like it should be pretty interesting. And it's from the same director as Prey, which I thought was excellent!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/\" target=\"_blank\">MrGone's Character Sheets</a><br /> For all your WoD Character Sheet Needs<br /> _________________________________<br /> Buy books &amp; pdfs from DTRPG and support my web site! <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=55414\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a><br /> Support my site on Patreon! <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mrgone\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24-mr-gone","name":"Mr Gone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-12T04:59:02-08:00","id":1556513,"title":"","content":"I've seen Predator Badlands a while ago (when it came out). Definitely would recommend in my opinion. A really fun movie. It was way better than I expected. <br /> <br /> The one I'm eager to see next is Avatar: Fire and Ash. Mostly, I'm just curious what the movie is even going to be about. I liked the first two movies (especially in terms of the visuals) but I really have no clue what else there is left to do in terms of storytelling. Especially because somehow these movies have been getting longer each time. Nearly three and a half hours is quite the length for a movie. <br /> <br /> I finished Tainted Grail: Fall of Avalon. It's essentially indie-Skyrim. It's clear it's a Skyrim-inspired game with a rather low budget. The mechanics range from janky to pretty good. And it's on the shorter side when it comes to length (compared to AAA-titles like Outer Worlds 2 or an Elder Scrolls). But it works quite well in two departments: Visuals and storytelling. Starting with the boardgame, the Tainted Grail franchise really had a lot of opportunities to develop its visual style and you see that in this game as well with how certain characters, regions and monsters look. In terms of storytelling, the game does a really good job of nailing its &quot;dark fantasy&quot;-vibe. For example, at the very start: Your character wakes up in a dungeon for the plague-ridden and somehow the soul of King Arthur gets attached to you who immediately starts to talk about saving Avalon. Then you meet another character who when he hears about this, tells you: &quot;Oh, you poor guy. They've been reviving King Arthur over and over in the past. He always ends up dying again. It never makes a difference. Things are just getting worse by the day.&quot; And the worldbuilding is quite good. To the point, there's pretty much an explanation for everything in the setting and why things are the way they are. <br /> <br /> Overall, I've played better games that do similar things before but for an indie-title, this one's pretty good. And it seems like the developer wants to add more content in the future. Despite its low budget, it's unexpected just how expansive and satisfying this game feels. As a Skyrim-esque game with dark-fantasy-flavor it's really good.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-12T08:39:47-08:00","id":1556517,"title":"","content":"With D&amp;D still not having put out its product schedule for 2026 yet, I\u2019ve really been getting into Curseborne and Earthbane, as well as Deadlands and Pendragon from other companies. These are all great games and you guys should definitely check them out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Amethyst is my birthstone. She/they.","edited":{"userid":26996,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst","user":"Amethyst","date":". 12-12-2025, 05:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst","name":"Amethyst","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-13T05:45:32-08:00","id":1556554,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502231-feel-free-to-gush?p=1556513#post1556513\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've seen Predator Badlands a while ago (when it came out). Definitely would recommend in my opinion. A really fun movie. It was way better than I expected.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh cool! Glad to hear you liked it! I'll hopefully get to see it soon!<br /> <br /> Oh, that animated Predator movie Killer of Killers was pretty good too!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502231-feel-free-to-gush?p=1556513#post1556513\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The one I'm eager to see next is Avatar: Fire and Ash. Mostly, I'm just curious what the movie is even going to be about. I liked the first two movies (especially in terms of the visuals) but I really have no clue what else there is left to do in terms of storytelling. Especially because somehow these movies have been getting longer each time. Nearly three and a half hours is quite the length for a movie.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've liked the 2 Avatar movies so far, but I think it's funny that James Cameron just wants to keep making them, because I'm not sure what else there is to do either. LOL! But, I guess I'll check em out!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502231-feel-free-to-gush?p=1556513#post1556513\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I finished Tainted Grail: Fall of Avalon. It's essentially indie-Skyrim. It's clear it's a Skyrim-inspired game with a rather low budget. The mechanics range from janky to pretty good. And it's on the shorter side when it comes to length (compared to AAA-titles like Outer Worlds 2 or an Elder Scrolls). But it works quite well in two departments: Visuals and storytelling. Starting with the boardgame, the Tainted Grail franchise really had a lot of opportunities to develop its visual style and you see that in this game as well with how certain characters, regions and monsters look. In terms of storytelling, the game does a really good job of nailing its &quot;dark fantasy&quot;-vibe. For example, at the very start: Your character wakes up in a dungeon for the plague-ridden and somehow the soul of King Arthur gets attached to you who immediately starts to talk about saving Avalon. Then you meet another character who when he hears about this, tells you: &quot;Oh, you poor guy. They've been reviving King Arthur over and over in the past. He always ends up dying again. It never makes a difference. Things are just getting worse by the day.&quot; And the worldbuilding is quite good. To the point, there's pretty much an explanation for everything in the setting and why things are the way they are.<br /> <br /> Overall, I've played better games that do similar things before but for an indie-title, this one's pretty good. And it seems like the developer wants to add more content in the future. Despite its low budget, it's unexpected just how expansive and satisfying this game feels. As a Skyrim-esque game with dark-fantasy-flavor it's really good.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks for the review! I haven't heard of that one, but I'll have to look into it..<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amethyst</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502231-feel-free-to-gush?p=1556517#post1556517\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">With D&amp;D still not having put out its product schedule for 2026 yet, I\u2019ve really been getting into Curseborne and Earthbane, as well as Deadlands and Pendragon from other companies. These are all great games and you guys should definitely check them out.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh nice! I just made a new character sheet for Curseborne, should you need one. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/\" target=\"_blank\">MrGone's Character Sheets</a><br /> For all your WoD Character Sheet Needs<br /> _________________________________<br /> Buy books &amp; pdfs from DTRPG and support my web site! <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=55414\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a><br /> Support my site on Patreon! <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mrgone\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24-mr-gone","name":"Mr Gone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-13T16:04:43-08:00","id":1556576,"title":"","content":"I just got the M:tA: Dead Magic Books and wow! I like them. I've never read such a clear description of Romans and Roman-society than in the Roman-Magic chapter. And they've got rules for actual, Mage: &quot;Liches&quot;. <br /> <br /> I also like the Norse-magic section; I've read the Ars Magica Norse-book, the Vampire: Dark Ages Norse-book and now this.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I have all the power in the world to give you, and all you have to do is beg&quot; -Nix<br /> <br /> &quot;There's thing about being a vampire, Frank; it takes a long fucking time to learn how do all the cool shit&quot;. -Abigail","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2521-iguazu","name":"Iguazu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2521_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"740"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-19T11:44:08-08:00","id":1556837,"title":"","content":"Seen two good movies. The first one was the newest entry in the Benoit Blanc series &quot;Wake Up Dead Man&quot;. Really liked Daniel Craig's recent turn post-Bond to play characters that are a bit more on the sillier side. Very different than the guy he played Guy Ritchie's Layer Cake all those years ago. Also liked his new look. He really reminded me of Mads Mikkelson which then made me think that he would be great as a Moriarty-like figure against Daniel Craig's Benoit Blanc. But the movie itself is a nice mystery-romp. The star-studded cast helps, of course. Particularly liked Josh O'Connor and Josh Brolin as the good and bad priest, respectively. The movie has a lot to say about present-day stuff but overall, I think the most noticeable thing is how hamfisted the movie is. It's a fun mystery-movie but the movie never shies away from being quite obvious about what you're supposed to think. <br /> <br /> Also saw Avatar: Fire and Ash. Visually still great. And the movie's a great spectacle in that regard. The action is still amazing, the family-stuff still works well and the talking whales are cool. It's just... I wish the movie had been a bit more daring with the story. This ash-tribe was really interesting because their homelands were close to a volcano. One day, it suddenly erupts and throws the tribe into chaos. And they're begging Ava for help but nothing happened. So they turned against Ava and are this more &quot;survival of the fittest&quot;-kind of brutal, martial tribe. I wish the movie had done more with that. I liked Oona Chaplin as Varang who's the leader of the ash tribe. Stephen Lang as Quaritch is also still really good. But in the end, it all amounts to it just being &quot;more of the same&quot;. I had a good time but yeah, if you liked the first two, you will like this one, too. But most of the beats in this third movie felt very familiar and well-trodden ground at this point. So I hope James Cameron will mix it up a little with the next one. <br /> <br /> Also saw the trailers of Christopher Nolan's next movie Odyssey. Can't wait to watch that! As for the trailer for Avengers: Doomsday... So they dragged Chris Evans back into the MCU again as well... sigh","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-20T05:48:12-08:00","id":1556855,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502231-feel-free-to-gush?p=1556837#post1556837\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Seen two good movies. The first one was the newest entry in the Benoit Blanc series &quot;Wake Up Dead Man&quot;. Really liked Daniel Craig's recent turn post-Bond to play characters that are a bit more on the sillier side. Very different than the guy he played Guy Ritchie's Layer Cake all those years ago. Also liked his new look. He really reminded me of Mads Mikkelson which then made me think that he would be great as a Moriarty-like figure against Daniel Craig's Benoit Blanc. But the movie itself is a nice mystery-romp. The star-studded cast helps, of course. Particularly liked Josh O'Connor and Josh Brolin as the good and bad priest, respectively. The movie has a lot to say about present-day stuff but overall, I think the most noticeable thing is how hamfisted the movie is. It's a fun mystery-movie but the movie never shies away from being quite obvious about what you're supposed to think.<br /> <br /> Also saw Avatar: Fire and Ash. Visually still great. And the movie's a great spectacle in that regard. The action is still amazing, the family-stuff still works well and the talking whales are cool. It's just... I wish the movie had been a bit more daring with the story. This ash-tribe was really interesting because their homelands were close to a volcano. One day, it suddenly erupts and throws the tribe into chaos. And they're begging Ava for help but nothing happened. So they turned against Ava and are this more &quot;survival of the fittest&quot;-kind of brutal, martial tribe. I wish the movie had done more with that. I liked Oona Chaplin as Varang who's the leader of the ash tribe. Stephen Lang as Quaritch is also still really good. But in the end, it all amounts to it just being &quot;more of the same&quot;. I had a good time but yeah, if you liked the first two, you will like this one, too. But most of the beats in this third movie felt very familiar and well-trodden ground at this point. So I hope James Cameron will mix it up a little with the next one.<br /> <br /> Also saw the trailers of Christopher Nolan's next movie Odyssey. Can't wait to watch that! As for the trailer for Avengers: Doomsday... So they dragged Chris Evans back into the MCU again as well... sigh</div> </div> </div> </div>I watched Wake Up Dead Man last weekend and highly enjoyed it! Daniel Craig is really owning the character of Benoit Blanc, so I'm glad that Rian Johnson has continued to make these movies! <br /> <br /> And I'm excited for the new Avatar movie. The last one was ok, but kind of just felt like setup for more movie, but it was still entertaining. And from the sounds of it it's at least as good as the others..","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/\" target=\"_blank\">MrGone's Character Sheets</a><br /> For all your WoD Character Sheet Needs<br /> _________________________________<br /> Buy books &amp; pdfs from DTRPG and support my web site! <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=55414\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a><br /> Support my site on Patreon! <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mrgone\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24-mr-gone","name":"Mr Gone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-22T18:41:00-08:00","id":1556926,"title":"","content":"I just saw the teaser trailer for Supergirl and my initial thoughts is that it looks promising with Kara being in a bad place dealing with the trauma of losing her people and planet and trying to drown her pain. Now I'm just a casual reader of Superman and his related titles but I do enjoy reading them from time to time.<br /> <br /> It's also looks like Lobo is going to have a role in the film, but what part he will play I don't know as it was just a teaser and we will know more down the road. I'm going to give this take on DCU by James Gunn a strong chance.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-24T17:48:38-08:00","id":1556973,"title":"","content":"The plot of Gunn's Supergirl is partially inspired in a very, <b>very</b> good comic arc called <i>Supergirl Woman of Tomorrow</i>, that I highly recommend by itself.<br /> <br /> Currently I'm finally delving deep on studying AI, a project I was without the energy for until recently. My main focus has been DeepSeek, although I plan on working with Gemini and ChatGPT very soon, and with Copilot once I get back to work.<br /> <br /> It's a shame that this is an economic bubble with companies operating at a loss, corporations focusing on how to use it to cut human cost instead of actually build something, and people expecting the next source of unverified claims to feed them dubious answers, because those are wonderful tools that can greatly increase our quality of life and ability to do not only work, but the things we enjoy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-29T04:19:40-08:00","id":1557088,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502231-feel-free-to-gush?p=1556926#post1556926\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I just saw the teaser trailer for Supergirl and my initial thoughts is that it looks promising with Kara being in a bad place dealing with the trauma of losing her people and planet and trying to drown her pain. Now I'm just a casual reader of Superman and his related titles but I do enjoy reading them from time to time.<br /> <br /> It's also looks like Lobo is going to have a role in the film, but what part he will play I don't know as it was just a teaser and we will know more down the road. I'm going to give this take on DCU by James Gunn a strong chance.</div> </div> </div> </div>I saw the teaser the other day and it looks great! I haven't read much Supergirl, but I'm pretty excited to see the movie!<br /> <br /> And I saw that second on Lobo in the teaser! I can't wait to see what they do with him in the movie!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/\" target=\"_blank\">MrGone's Character Sheets</a><br /> For all your WoD Character Sheet Needs<br /> _________________________________<br /> Buy books &amp; pdfs from DTRPG and support my web site! <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=55414\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a><br /> Support my site on Patreon! <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mrgone\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24-mr-gone","name":"Mr Gone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-30T17:24:28-08:00","id":1557159,"title":"","content":"I managed to see Marty Supreme before the end of the year and good thing I did. This is definitely one of my favorite movies of 2025. Somewhere in the middle I thought &quot;This feels like an upbeat version of Uncut Gems.&quot; and then at the end when the credits rolled, I saw that one of the Safdie Brothers co-wrote the screenplay and also was the director of the movie. Timothee Chalamet is great as the main-character. I don't even know how to categorize him. Anti-hero doesn't quite fit. To be honest, the imagery that came to mind for me to characterize him was a cannonball. Destructive, ever-moving... that sort of thing. Chalamet's character is an asshole. But when he's facing the stoic table-tennis-player at the end and pretty much everyones watching him (within the film) wants him to lose, you just can't help but cheer for him. I think the most compelling part of the movie is that Chalamet is an asshole for acting like he's the main-character of the universe - except he is. And at the same time: That character's life sucks and he made the lives of everybody he interacted with worse. But hell, what a ride! Great movie!<br /> <br /> Also saw the second volume of Stranger Things Season Five... I liked this one more than the first part. But especially the part between Nancy and Jonathan made me realize just how much of a wasted opportunity Jonathan's character has been. Charlie Heaton (as Jonathan) is actually a pretty good actor, it turns out. But I know why I only notice it now because he had been sidelined for quite a while in past seasons. Other than that... Honestly, I wish the real finale had actually just come out with this batch of episodes. Just let's get it over with.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-31T19:26:52-08:00","id":1557168,"title":"","content":"The final episode of Stranger Things was amazing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Amethyst is my birthstone. She/they.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst","name":"Amethyst","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-02T11:55:35-08:00","id":1557209,"title":"","content":"I decided to pick up the entire Jurassic Park series minus the one with Scarlett Johansson as it wasn't around in the store and I will get it later. I like to see how much the special effects have improved since the first film.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-03T05:30:56-08:00","id":1557228,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502231-feel-free-to-gush?p=1557209#post1557209\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I decided to pick up the entire Jurassic Park series minus the one with Scarlett Johansson as it wasn't around in the store and I will get it later. I like to see how much the special effects have improved since the first film.</div> </div> </div> </div>Funny enough, the special effects kinda peaked with the first one. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> The newer Jurassic World movies are ok (and the effects are pretty good)... but they ended up doing something I think they regretted and then spent like the last two or 3 movies trying to walk it back. It's crazy.<br /> <br /> Oh, and that new one with Scarlett Johansson reminded me a lot of Jurassic Park 3. When you finally do see it, you'll see what I mean. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/\" target=\"_blank\">MrGone's Character Sheets</a><br /> For all your WoD Character Sheet Needs<br /> _________________________________<br /> Buy books &amp; pdfs from DTRPG and support my web site! <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=55414\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a><br /> Support my site on Patreon! <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mrgone\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24-mr-gone","name":"Mr Gone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-05T02:30:03-08:00","id":1557300,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502231-feel-free-to-gush?p=1557209#post1557209\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">. I like to see how much the special effects have improved since the first film.</div> </div> </div> </div>Won't see much.<br /> <br /> Special effects aren't about technology. Tech helps a lot, sure, but mainly to make it cheaper and faster, and the first movie had too much money for this to be a concern.<br /> <br /> Really what makes good special effects is artistry. Is the team behind it knowing how to deliver <i>an experience</i>. And you'll hardly see a better team than what Spielberg got in the first movie.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-05T17:20:21-08:00","id":1557322,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr Gone</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502231-feel-free-to-gush?p=1557088#post1557088\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I saw the teaser the other day and it looks great! I haven't read much Supergirl, but I'm pretty excited to see the movie <br /> <br /> Same here but I do know the core elements of her origin and sometime ago I bought The Superman Encyclopedia and The Batman Encyclopedia to learn more things about the characters published history and more stuff I wasn't clear on.<br /> <br /> While I'm a big Batman fan, I will admit that I do have gaps in my knowledge about his lore and various facts. It's a big help and I will probably will see if they have a Wonder Woman Encyclopedia around.<br /> <br /> And I saw that second on Lobo in the teaser! I can't wait to see what they do with him in the movie!</div> </div> </div> </div>It should be interesting to see as I learned that this film is inspired by Supergirl Woman of Tomorrow and I need to read it.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-06T00:53:28-08:00","id":1557333,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502231-feel-free-to-gush?p=1557322#post1557322\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It should be interesting to see as I learned that this film is inspired by Supergirl Woman of Tomorrow and I need to read it.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Inspired, but isn't meant to be the same or even similar story. Yet I have good expectations for the movie.<br /> <br /> And seriously, go read Woman of Tomorrow, it's pure gold.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-06T13:43:19-08:00","id":1557353,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502231-feel-free-to-gush?p=1557322#post1557322\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It should be interesting to see as I learned that this film is inspired by Supergirl Woman of Tomorrow and I need to read it.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, that's cool! I've heard that story is really good, but I haven't read it either. Might need to check it out. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/\" target=\"_blank\">MrGone's Character Sheets</a><br /> For all your WoD Character Sheet Needs<br /> _________________________________<br /> Buy books &amp; pdfs from DTRPG and support my web site! <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=55414\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a><br /> Support my site on Patreon! <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mrgone\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24-mr-gone","name":"Mr Gone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-21T22:03:08-08:00","id":1557823,"title":"","content":"I recently did pick up and read Supergirl Woman of Tomorrow and it's is a great read and I can see some of the scenes from the teaser trailer that it's drawn from. But how closely it will follow the book is a different story.<br /> <br /> Lobo doesn't appear in the comic, but I did hear that Tom King wanted to use him in the book and wasn't able to.<br /> <br /> Either way it is making me more inclined to want to watch the film when it does come out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-29T05:05:08-08:00","id":1557985,"title":"","content":"Really enjoying Fallout season 2 so far. It's a bit different from the games' lore but it's still a great show. Walton Goggins is of course always great and Kyle Machlachan is pretty good as well. But the whole cast is great. And the show clearly has a big budget. The show is just really good at nailing that vibe-mix of comedy and serious drama. I especially like Johnny Pemberton as Thaddeus. That's a really fun performance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-29T15:58:33-08:00","id":1558000,"title":"","content":"I'm curious to see Batman 2 by Matt Reeves and see how he will depict Two-Face and what character Scarlet Johasen will be playing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-30T02:49:12-08:00","id":1558015,"title":"","content":"What I'm even more curious about is how they're going to handle Batman going forward. Because <a href=\"https://www.denofgeek.com/tv/james-gunn-absolutely-shuts-down-speculation-about-robert-pattinsons-batman/\" target=\"_blank\">James Gunn recently said</a> that Robert Pattinson won't play Batman in the wider DC-movie-universe. I mean, I get it. Robert Pattinson probably doesn't want to bind himself to this kind of comic-book-movie-universe. But I wonder how this is supposed to work if there are supposed to be even more Batman movies with Matt Reeves as the director and Pattinson as Batman. <br /> <br /> I liked that first Matt Reeves Batman and the Penguin TV show they made based on that, so I'm looking forward to what they're going to do with the sequel<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-30T15:23:36-08:00","id":1558031,"title":"","content":"The DC animated shows had multiple continuities going at once, and we had the TV shows completely separate from the movies too; and the comics themselves are no strangers to this either.<br /> <br /> I don't think Gunn or the audience are going to struggle with, &quot;Reeves and Pattison's stuff is great and will continue so it can be it's own awesome thing, but a separate continuity from the new shared universe that's the main movies we're working on.&quot; The WBD suits that made so many bad calls previously are the people that don't understand that it's very easy to do that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-31T02:39:04-08:00","id":1558039,"title":"","content":"What I mean is, couldn't it become an issue if you have the Reeves-Batman with Pattinson as Batman and then there's a Justice League movie coming out that has a different actor playing Batman and the fans of the former won't go to the theater to watch the latter because they don't like the other version of the character? Also, is the goal to do something like the MCU or is James Gunn just gonna oversee the production of various not necessarily related movies using the DC-Comics-IP?<br /> <br /> But also, you're right that even if the first thing I mentioned might become an issue, it still very well might end up doing better than the mess that has been the previous DC-movies-era. Not just the Zack Snyder of it all but movies like The Flash or Wonder Woman 1984... oof, some of those were rough to sit through.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-31T05:28:18-08:00","id":1558042,"title":"","content":"It's only a problem if it's a problem really?<br /> <br /> Spider-man fans were not upset when the Miles focused animated movies started overlapping with the MCU Tom Holland Peter focused movies; even with characters existing in both continuities but obviously completely different versions.<br /> <br /> If Gunn greenlights a shit Batman... the problem is a shit Batman, not the existence of good Batman movies separate from the new main DC cinematic universe. If both Batmen are good, the fans will come out for both.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-02-01T23:11:35-08:00","id":1558060,"title":"","content":"I don't see the issue of Robert Pattinson only playing Batman one more time is going to be a problem and having a different actor playing the Caped Crusader in the future.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-02-02T00:13:01-08:00","id":1558061,"title":"","content":"I honestly hope they do more than just one more... but if that's what Reeves and Pattinson thing is good I'm not going to argue against it.<br /> <br /> I think it's a great chance for Gunn to reassert something that made DC a much stronger franchise than Marvel when it came to their non-comic media up until the MCU, and now after everyone's a bit tired of the MCU: having stuff to watch that doesn't require giving up multiple weekends to binging to catch up on what you need to know to get into it. That's one of the reasons why the DC animated shows were so beloved. The quality is generally high, but also there wasn't a hard joined single universe where everything was getting impacted by everything else. You didn't have to worry about watching Justice League Unlimited to know what was going on in the separate Batman animated show at the same time.<br /> <br /> I really do think fans will reward DC/WBD is Gunn is given the freedom to do &quot;side&quot; continuities that are low bars of entry for casual fans that are still enjoyable for hardcore fans; even hardcore fans want a break from deep diving into the 20th movie in an ongoing franchise.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-02-02T01:13:42-08:00","id":1558062,"title":"","content":"I would have loved to see what James Gunn could have done with Simon Williams aka Wonder Man or other c list characters from Marvel Comics. But Marvel Comics loss is DC Comics gain.<br /> <br /> Yes I'm aware that they did a live action version of Wonder Man and I haven't seen it yet.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-02-02T12:21:39-08:00","id":1558082,"title":"","content":"On a more pleasant note I got a really good b movie present from my buddies. I have Army of Darkness by Sam Raimi and I haven't watched this film in years and remembered how cool of character that Ash is played by Bruce Campbell.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-02-03T16:14:11-08:00","id":1558101,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502231-feel-free-to-gush?p=1558062#post1558062\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes I'm aware that they did a live action version of Wonder Man and I haven't seen it yet.</div> </div> </div> </div>I just finished the series last night and thought it was excellent! I don't know much about the character, but I'm sure they changed up quite a bit about him. But, I thought the show was a lot of fun and I hope they do another season, or do more with that character in the future!<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/\" target=\"_blank\">MrGone's Character Sheets</a><br /> For all your WoD Character Sheet Needs<br /> _________________________________<br /> Buy books &amp; pdfs from DTRPG and support my web site! <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=55414\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a><br /> Support my site on Patreon! <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mrgone\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24-mr-gone","name":"Mr Gone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-02-03T19:13:32-08:00","id":1558104,"title":"","content":"While I'm a much bigger fan of DC Comics in general, I have to admit I'm intrigued by Avengers Doomsday and if the theories of how Robert Downey Jr can be Dr. Doom as well as Iron Man.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-02-03T20:42:34-08:00","id":1558105,"title":"","content":"Mr Gone from what I can remember about Simon Williams was that he and and brother Eric were from a wealthy family and Simon Williams took up the family business and I think it was weapons manufacturing.<br /> <br /> He ran into some trouble and agreed to be experimented on by Baron Zemo and got vast superhuman strength and durability via ionic energy and was set to fight the Avengers.<br /> <br /> He reformed and joined the team in varying capacities for both the East Coast and West Coast teams. I'm really showing my age here.<br /> <br /> I'm sure that they will ignore his relationship with Scarlett Witch and that he and Vision are quasi siblings as it was his mental patterns that was used to give the Vision intelligence. If I recall Simon Williams was in a comma at the time and wasn't expected to recover.<br /> <br /> I know comics can get very strange with character creation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":27361,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","user":"Lysander","date":". 02-04-2026, 01:01 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-02-03T21:03:28-08:00","id":1558106,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr Gone</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502231-feel-free-to-gush?p=1558101#post1558101\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I just finished the series last night and thought it was excellent! I don't know much about the character, but I'm sure they changed up quite a bit about him. But, I thought the show was a lot of fun and I hope they do another season, or do more with that character in the future!<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>It's kinda weird because there's a lot that was changed for sure, but a lot of it came from Wonder Man being such a product of the wider Marvel universe at the time (he was written with a background that connected him to a lot of existing characters). I think the show benefits a lot from a much more stripped down version of the character that didn't play up being interconnected with so many others (though the show left open a lot of possible ways to work those connections in) and rearranging some of the quintessential character beats that makes him tick.<br /> <br /> Though I have to admit I'm going to be very amused if the show gets enough seasons to do the canon storyline after he gives up trying to balance acting and being a superhero... because being canon accurate is going to lead to a lot of very dumb comments about Disney ruining the character for &quot;political&quot; reasons despite, you know, just sticking to the comics. Kinda like how people were tying themselves in knots to try to justify having The Falcon take over as Captain America as some sort of diversity thing instead of just... being what happened in the comics.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-02-03T21:06:58-08:00","id":1558107,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502231-feel-free-to-gush?p=1558105#post1558105\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm sure that they will ignore his relationship with Scarlett Witch and that he and Vision are quasi siblings as it was his mental patterns that was used to give the Vision intelligence.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've seen a lot of speculation that they might reverse this and have Simon's powers come from the white Vision that appeared in Wandavision. Though I'd imagine that would depend a lot of if Paul Bettany wants to be involved.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-02-03T22:00:02-08:00","id":1558109,"title":"","content":"There's lots of speculation about Avengers Doomsday and it's what makes it fun, but we will have to wait and see how it will unfold. It sucks that Media Grifters like Kinnel and Critical Drinker go full mask off whenever they see a female character or some person with darker colored skin and disparge them. They just move the goal posts and I will leave it there as it veers into the vent thread.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-02-05T16:24:26-08:00","id":1558122,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502231-feel-free-to-gush?p=1558106#post1558106\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's kinda weird because there's a lot that was changed for sure, but a lot of it came from Wonder Man being such a product of the wider Marvel universe at the time (he was written with a background that connected him to a lot of existing characters). I think the show benefits a lot from a much more stripped down version of the character that didn't play up being interconnected with so many others (though the show left open a lot of possible ways to work those connections in) and rearranging some of the quintessential character beats that makes him tick.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yea, I like this more stripped down version. It made sense for the story they were doing, and I liked the connection to Trevor, and then that opens him up to the wider MCU from there.<br /> <br /> But I thought the series was great. But, I'm a sucker for behind the scenes Hollywood stuff sometimes.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502231-feel-free-to-gush?p=1558106#post1558106\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Though I have to admit I'm going to be very amused if the show gets enough seasons to do the canon storyline after he gives up trying to balance acting and being a superhero... because being canon accurate is going to lead to a lot of very dumb comments about Disney ruining the character for &quot;political&quot; reasons despite, you know, just sticking to the comics. Kinda like how people were tying themselves in knots to try to justify having The Falcon take over as Captain America as some sort of diversity thing instead of just... being what happened in the comics.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, I have no doubt that people are gonna be assholes about it eventually. They always are. But, I really hope they do a few more seasons of this show. I guess I won't hold my breath, but it'd be awesome. If nothing else hopefully they'll at least use the character somewhere else..<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/\" target=\"_blank\">MrGone's Character Sheets</a><br /> For all your WoD Character Sheet Needs<br /> _________________________________<br /> Buy books &amp; pdfs from DTRPG and support my web site! <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=55414\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a><br /> Support my site on Patreon! <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mrgone\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24-mr-gone","name":"Mr Gone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-02-05T16:25:40-08:00","id":1558123,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502231-feel-free-to-gush?p=1558105#post1558105\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mr Gone from what I can remember about Simon Williams was that he and and brother Eric were from a wealthy family and Simon Williams took up the family business and I think it was weapons manufacturing.<br /> <br /> He ran into some trouble and agreed to be experimented on by Baron Zemo and got vast superhuman strength and durability via ionic energy and was set to fight the Avengers.<br /> <br /> He reformed and joined the team in varying capacities for both the East Coast and West Coast teams. I'm really showing my age here.<br /> <br /> I'm sure that they will ignore his relationship with Scarlett Witch and that he and Vision are quasi siblings as it was his mental patterns that was used to give the Vision intelligence. If I recall Simon Williams was in a comma at the time and wasn't expected to recover.<br /> <br /> I know comics can get very strange with character creation.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh whoa! That's pretty crazy! Yea, gotta love comics sometimes, they can be so weird and convoluted. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/\" target=\"_blank\">MrGone's Character Sheets</a><br /> For all your WoD Character Sheet Needs<br /> _________________________________<br /> Buy books &amp; pdfs from DTRPG and support my web site! <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=55414\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a><br /> Support my site on Patreon! <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mrgone\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude0e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24-mr-gone","name":"Mr Gone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-02-06T10:48:25-08:00","id":1558143,"title":"","content":"Another movie I'm looking forward to is Christopher Nolan The Odyssey and see how he will bring the epic to light and it has an impressive cast.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-02-07T03:38:03-08:00","id":1558160,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div clas