he one who tried to kill Snake Eyes.<br /> <br /> But this created new problems as people pointed out is why Zartan was there as neither GI-Joe or Cobra wasn't around yet and what was the reasoning for it. Enter the future Cobra Commander who's brother died driving the influence and killed the family of Snake Eyes in a car accident and couldn't accept the fact of how messed up his older brother was and blamed the victims.<br /> <br /> Talk about a crazy stuff back in the day.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ha! LOL! Gotta love a good retcon! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Comics are fun though, and with a long enough running continuity there is bound to be a lot of weirdness..","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/\" target=\"_blank\">MrGone's Character Sheets</a><br /> For all your WoD Character Sheet Needs<br /> _________________________________<br /> Buy books &amp; pdfs from DTRPG and support my web site! <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=55414\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a><br /> Support my site on Patreon! <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mrgone\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24-mr-gone","name":"Mr Gone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-02-11T18:40:03-08:00","id":1558247,"title":"","content":"Watching Jamestown (PBS-series). It's a good show, but, despite liking Shakespeare's times, I'm just now willing to devote the time to watch it. Tomorrow, it's due back at the library; In other news!!! I got Hexen working on my desktop. I just uploaded DeathKings; now, I have to find my Hexen Wad CD that had a bunch of extra levels to play on it as well as a level-editor; Back in the day, I grew frustrated with it, but I was impressed by editing blowing-leaves.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I have all the power in the world to give you, and all you have to do is beg&quot; -Nix<br /> <br /> &quot;There's thing about being a vampire, Frank; it takes a long fucking time to learn how do all the cool shit&quot;. -Abigail","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2521-iguazu","name":"Iguazu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2521_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"740"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-02-12T16:28:10-08:00","id":1558267,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr Gone</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502231-feel-free-to-gush?p=1558242#post1558242\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ha! LOL! Gotta love a good retcon! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Comics are fun though, and with a long enough running continuity there is bound to be a lot of weirdness..</div> </div> </div> </div>I forgot to mention that Cobra Commander was the one who hired Zartan to do the job and it showed how he got close to the clan by working as a master blacksmith apprentice and started really enjoying the job and almost didn't go through the assassination because of it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude02","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-02-13T13:31:11-08:00","id":1558293,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502231-feel-free-to-gush?p=1558267#post1558267\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I forgot to mention that Cobra Commander was the one who hired Zartan to do the job and it showed how he got close to the clan by working as a master blacksmith apprentice and started really enjoying the job and almost didn't go through the assassination because of it.</div> </div> </div> </div>LOL! That's crazy! Comics are great sometimes...<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/\" target=\"_blank\">MrGone's Character Sheets</a><br /> For all your WoD Character Sheet Needs<br /> _________________________________<br /> Buy books &amp; pdfs from DTRPG and support my web site! <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=55414\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a><br /> Support my site on Patreon! <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mrgone\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24-mr-gone","name":"Mr Gone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-02-22T06:40:07-08:00","id":1558446,"title":"","content":"Really enjoying &quot;Knight of the Seven Kingdoms&quot; so far. Feels like the good ol' days when Game Of Thrones was still an interesting show.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-02-23T18:12:34-08:00","id":1558475,"title":"","content":"I get a lot of my food, from a soup-kitchen, so I rarely have to set foot in a grocery-store, besides the fact I get EBT, so, I like have a back-up for my back-up.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I have all the power in the world to give you, and all you have to do is beg&quot; -Nix<br /> <br /> &quot;There's thing about being a vampire, Frank; it takes a long fucking time to learn how do all the cool shit&quot;. -Abigail","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2521-iguazu","name":"Iguazu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2521_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"740"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-02-24T17:51:24-08:00","id":1558505,"title":"","content":"Having a good week this week. Played a game of Vampire the Masquerade 20th Anniversary for the first time in a long time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Amethyst is my birthstone. She/they.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst","name":"Amethyst","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-03-02T04:37:56-08:00","id":1558584,"title":"","content":"I just recently watched Predator Badlands and I really liked it and enjoyed seeing it from the perspective of Dek who is a runt by his species standards is still larger and physically more powerful than the most fit human.<br /> <br /> I also liked it that it takes place in the future where humanity is exploring outer space and we have synthetic beings and cementing the ties to the Aliens universe.<br /> <br /> Another thing I liked is that we saw how Dek grows as a character and starts to listen to his late brother Kwei advice of playing to your strengths and using the environment to your advantage and we see Thia also reinforce the point as he is in a strange planet of Gehenna that he knows really nothing about other then what his older brother told him that no member of the Yjanti has completed a hunt for the Kraslok ( forgive my spelling mistakes) .<br /> <br /> I do enjoy the quips and one liners in the film and it reminded me of what the first movie was like. A fact that many people who lambasted Badlands for have forgotten about and I'm sure if I rewatch Predator 2 again and Danny Glover will utter his iconic &quot;I'm getting to old for this sh3t.&quot;<br /> <br /> Before Badlands and Prey, I thought the film series was done and seeing Badlands was the shot to the arm it needed to revive interest in the IP and I'm curious to see what Dek's Mom is going to be like.<br /> <br /> <br /> As a casual fan of the Predator I don't know lots about the lore that Darkhorse Comics and some of the related novels that fleshed out the back story of the species and what they are called. It sounds like that I will have to buy some back issues. Now I plan on watching Prey and see how much I hope to like it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":27361,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","user":"Lysander","date":". 03-08-2026, 11:02 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-03-03T18:49:44-08:00","id":1558628,"title":"","content":"I watched Predator Prey and found it a enjoyable film and it reminded me why I liked the series in general. I appreciate that it was set in the early 18th century with the Commanche tribe as the protagonist going up against a threat outside their experience. It reminds me that the theme is close to what the First Predator film was about.<br /> <br /> You know you have experienced hunters in this case instead of special forces operatives going up against a larger more technological advanced foe and they need to work together and outsmart it and use the environment to there advantage.<br /> <br /> I'll have to reread my books on the Commanche tribe to refresh my memory and see what creative liberty they took.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-03-07T15:34:29-08:00","id":1558714,"title":"","content":"I've been playing Slay The Spire II since it came out. Man, another great indie-game-sequel that actually is a proper sequel. I've been having a great time with it so far.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502231-feel-free-to-gush?p=1558628#post1558628\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I watched Predator Prey and found it a enjoyable film and it reminded me why I liked the series in general. I appreciate that it was set in the early 18th century with the Commanche tribe as the protagonist going up against a threat outside their experience. It reminds me that the theme is close to what the First Predator film was about.<br /> <br /> You know you have experienced hunters in this case instead of special forces operatives going up against a larger more technological advanced foe and they need to work together and outsmart it and use the environment to there advantage.<br /> <br /> I'll have to reread my books on the Commanche tribe to refresh my memory and see what creative liberty they took.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Have you also seen the animated movie Predator: Killer of Killers from last year? The same director as for Prey and Badlands (Dan Trechtenberg) was also involved in that one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-03-07T17:20:04-08:00","id":1558717,"title":"","content":"No I haven't Knightingale and I will have to look out for it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-03-07T17:45:10-08:00","id":1558720,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502231-feel-free-to-gush?p=1558717#post1558717\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No I haven't Knightingale and I will have to look out for it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, okay. I recommend, you should because that movie does hint at there being a &quot;shared universe&quot;, let's say <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> . Considering that Dan Trechtenberg was involved with Prey, that animated movie &quot;Killer of Killers&quot; AND Badlands, it does seem like he's overseeing the IP (under Disney, of course). So, it wouldn't surprise me if a future film were to be released with the assumption that you had seen all three movies before.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-03-07T20:16:56-08:00","id":1558724,"title":"","content":"Technically it's under 20th Century Studios, but Disney does own them. I also see that Masters of the Universe trailer came out and it looks interesting but I'm not sold on Jared Leto as Skeletor. Though I can't find a actor who could play old skull \ud83d\udc80 face.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-03-08T05:55:15-07:00","id":1558728,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar27361_11.jpg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"27361\" data-vbnamecard=\"27361\">Lysander</a> , glad to hear you liked Prey and Preador: Badlands! I thought they were both really good! Dan Trechtenberg is doing an amazing job with this series now! But I saw Badlands pretty recently and absolutely loved it! It was cool having a Yautja being the protagonist, and seeing how he learned and grew over the course of the story. Elle Fanning was great as the synthetic too!<br /> <br /> As for Prey, I highly enjoyed it too. I need to rewatch it again. I first watched in English, but I need to check out that Comanche version.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502231-feel-free-to-gush?p=1558720#post1558720\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ah, okay. I recommend, you should because that movie does hint at there being a &quot;shared universe&quot;, let's say <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> . Considering that Dan Trechtenberg was involved with Prey, that animated movie &quot;Killer of Killers&quot; AND Badlands, it does seem like he's overseeing the IP (under Disney, of course). So, it wouldn't surprise me if a future film were to be released with the assumption that you had seen all three movies before.</div> </div> </div> </div>I second Killer of Killers! It was great! And the ending had some pretty crazy implications!<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/\" target=\"_blank\">MrGone's Character Sheets</a><br /> For all your WoD Character Sheet Needs<br /> _________________________________<br /> Buy books &amp; pdfs from DTRPG and support my web site! <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=55414\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a><br /> Support my site on Patreon! <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mrgone\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24-mr-gone","name":"Mr Gone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-03-19T17:58:24-07:00","id":1558945,"title":"","content":"I love this V20 Play By Post I'm playing in on another site alongside my hubby, we're with a really good group and he can play it at a leisurely place.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm just a trans guy and gaming fan, unabashed hedonist and unusually upbeat nihilist, fairly laid back. He/Him.<br /> <br /> If everything is political, then nothing is!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25920-matt-corleone","name":"Matt Corleone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25920_8.webp","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-03-29T11:22:26-07:00","id":1559098,"title":"","content":"On a brighter note. I recently watched the movie Caught Stealing with Austin Butler, Zoe Kravitz, Regina King, Liev Schreiber, Vincent De Nofrio and Matt Smith who was sporting a cool punk mohawk and wardrobe.<br /> <br /> It's a heist thriller set in 1998 New York and I liked how they tried to recreate the world where people had to use payphones and didn't have a cellphone glued to their ear.<br /> <br /> Austin Butler plays a bartender who agreed to look after his neighbor cat played by Matt Smith and finds himself being chased after Russian and Jewish mobsters because of it.<br /> <br /> Turns out Matt Smith stole 4 million from them and they want it back and take the cat hostage.<br /> <br /> Austin Butler does a good job playing a normal guy who isn't a one man army and gets hurt when is in a fight and you can buy the notion of him being a an ex baseball player who might have been a superstar but squandered due to substance abuse. <br /> I found this movie good and I won't go any further to spoil the rest of the film in case you haven't watched it.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"ht