mrgone\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24-mr-gone","name":"Mr Gone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-04-30T17:44:36-07:00","id":1559685,"title":"","content":"I've been watching a YouTube personality going by the name of Chris Star Wars Legends with my favorite star wars character Grand Admiral Thrawn doing a deep dive why the empire failed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-05-01T04:37:58-07:00","id":1559686,"title":"","content":"Rest In Power <br /> David Allan Coe<br /> 1939-2026<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=LZbso7sNqv0\" data-code=\"LZbso7sNqv0\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/LZbso7sNqv0/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> <br /> The dude was a truly talented musician and one of the great outlaws of country music, and he was also an outspoken advocate of the LGBTQ community at a time where that was rare and got him in hot water with the Nashville establishment. The dude literally made a foul-mouthed diss track targeted at Anita Bryant after she went on her crusade against gays in the 70's and it's one of my favorites.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=nBikZ8sRzxQ&amp;rco=1\" data-code=\"nBikZ8sRzxQ\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/nBikZ8sRzxQ/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm just a trans guy and gaming fan, unabashed hedonist and unusually upbeat nihilist, fairly laid back. He/Him.<br /> <br /> If everything is political, then nothing is!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25920-matt-corleone","name":"Matt Corleone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25920_8.webp","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-05-05T11:38:15-07:00","id":1559792,"title":"","content":"I know it's wrong to celebrate the misfortune of others, but I would be lying if I'm not enjoying the downfall of unhinged conspiracy grifter Alex Jones and that Infowars might be owned by the satire news site the Onion. If the Onion does get Infowars they promise to make sure that the families of Sandy Hook will get their money \ud83d\udcb8\ud83d\udcb0.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-05-06T09:04:13-07:00","id":1559809,"title":"","content":"So deeply enjoying the latest music from Rob Zombie and Megadeth.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-05-07T11:36:31-07:00","id":1559823,"title":"","content":"More of a repeat of previous topic, but I must say that the YouTube channel Chris Star Wars Legend is really good and he really understands the motivation and character of Grand Admiral Thrawn, Palleon, Karrade..<br /> <br /> His take on Grand Admiral Thrawn is really good and shows how Timothy Zahn depicted him in the Legends/Expanded universe line.<br /> <br /> He talks why the Jedi, Republic, Sith and the Empire failed and how he was going to be different with his version of the Empire.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-05-12T06:50:51-07:00","id":1559900,"title":"","content":"Saw Mortal Kombat II and it was way better than I expected. Not a great movie but a fun one. Especially compared to the first movie. Then again, what made this one work is that it just started to stick really close to the games. For example, that new character they invented in the first movie named Cole was immediately sidelined - and thank God, they did. That character was such a bore. Karl Urban as Johnny Cage was good, but not great. I think I'd have preferred if they had stuck closer to the games there as well. In this version, with Karl Urban playing the character it's more about him an aging actor who's past his prime. Also, the plot is ludicrously straightforward and things get set up in record-time in order to get to the fighting as soon as possible. But then again, the movie does have great action-sequences, so it's not like I was complaining about the fact that the movie barely couldn't wait to throw the characters into these action-sequences.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-05-15T09:48:10-07:00","id":1559989,"title":"","content":"I hope Transformers by Image Comics will continue to bring more screen time for lesser known characters like Blue Streak, Tracks, Mindwipe, and the Predacons. They have given a fair amount of of screen time to Elita 1 of the Autobots and I would like to see more female Autobots like her and hopefully some Decepticons that will be made hopefully.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-05-16T20:03:31-07:00","id":1560038,"title":"","content":"Uhh, guys, there was a black bear in my yard earlier this evening.<br /> <br /> It was small enough to be mistaken for a very shaggy dog at first, so I think it might have been a cub. But I don't know how big a black bear is supposed to be when it's fully grown. If it did have a mother nearby, she thankfully decided not to reveal herself.<br /> <br /> <br /> To the best of my knowledge, this is the second time a bear has come sniffing around our house in recent history. The first time my brother said he saw one, but the rest of us were asleep at the time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-05-16T23:22:36-07:00","id":1560039,"title":"","content":"Black bears aren't that big by bear standards. An adult is going to top out around 3ft at the shoulder and 6ft long. They are very fast and can weight a lot for that size though. It's worth looking up the bears where you live as the black bear has a lot of regional subspecies that can change what to expect.<br /> <br /> In general though, black bears don't usually cause a lot of trouble for humans as long as you give them space. Since adult humans can easily be a similar size to them, and they tend to be skittish as they're too small to take on brown bears or packs of canines, they'd rather run than fight. So it's important not to corner them. They are, however, very human acclimated so if they feel safe around your property they're going to keep coming back in the hopes of easy snacks from trash cans and the like. It can be a good idea to call local wildlife services and see if they have anyone that does humane relocation and will move the bear(s) into a better protected area before a confrontation with humans happens.<br /> <br /> If you see one trying to get into your house, or one of your neighbor's houses - or even sheds or other detached buildings - you need to call the local wildlife authorities ASAP. That's when they need to get relocated as trouble can happen real fast if they sneak into places humans already are or might come into without realizing what's going on. My grandparents got really lucky when they used to life in an area with a lot of black bears. They had been gone for two weeks, and one broke into their house seeming to have realized nobody was home for awhile. They got home and thought they'd been robbed until the bear ran past them and outside. You can imagine how easily that could have gone not good. Fortunately for the bear too, he was caught and relocated safely to a state park about two hours away from human homes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-02T14:27:18-07:00","id":1560314,"title":"","content":"I have just discovered that <b>Ars Magica</b>, the spiritual precursor to <b>Mage: the Ascension</b>, had an entire house of Hermetics that were just autistically focused on using magic to become their spiritual fursona. Even to the point where they considered the study of hermetic magic to be less important in comparison.<br /> <br /> Honestly, I can respect the simplicity of that. They know what they want out of life, and they won't suffer any distractions!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29027-greathornedratkin","name":"GreatHornedRatkin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29027_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2026"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-03T15:41:31-07:00","id":1560328,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GreatHornedRatkin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502231-feel-free-to-gush?p=1560314#post1560314\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have just discovered that <b>Ars Magica</b>, the spiritual precursor to <b>Mage: the Ascension</b>, had an entire house of Hermetics that were just autistically focused on using magic to become their spiritual fursona. Even to the point where they considered the study of hermetic magic to be less important in comparison.<br /> <br /> Honestly, I can respect the simplicity of that. They know what they want out of life, and they won't suffer any distractions!</div> </div> </div> </div>YES! I'm looking into getting a hard-copy of <i>Ars Magica</i>. It's book background material for Order of Hermes. But, I'm not liking the game-system for <i>Ars Magica. Dark Ages: Mage</i>, is basically a revised, version of <i>Ars Magica</i>, except with Vampires and Werewolves.<br /> <br /> <br /> And <i>Ars Magica</i>'s Viking's book, was great!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I have all the power in the world to give you, and all you have to do is beg&quot; -Nix<br /> <br /> &quot;There's thing about being a vampire, Frank; it takes a long fucking time to learn how do all the cool shit&quot;. -Abigail","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2521-iguazu","name":"Iguazu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2521_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"740"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-03T19:03:52-07:00","id":1560330,"title":"","content":"Congratulations on the James Bond Lost Light game being a successful seller. As a fan of the character it's always good to see it being well liked from all types.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs 