arscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-05T22:09:40-07:00","id":1560400,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkKing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502231-feel-free-to-gush?p=1560395#post1560395\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ageless sharks, and people transforming into dinosaurs.<br /> <br /> Older Werewolf was metal AF.</div> </div> </div> </div>Rokea weren't specifically noted as being ageless until the 2nd edition player's guide. One of those &quot;what do you mean we didn't mention that?&quot; things.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Your lucky to avoid watching Kindred The Embraced Iguaza all together. It was not even on the level of a guilty pleasure viewing bad and I don't think Space Ice or Mystery Science Theatre 3000 could make it good.</div> </div> </div> </div>I disagree; the actor allusions alone would be hilarious in a riff show. Sasha was played by the same actress that portrayed Thina in Quest of the Delta Knights, Brian Thompson (who was in almost everything) was Eddie Fiori, and as for Sonny, well, Surprise, Motherfucker!<br /> <br /> There's also the obligatory jokes about Nosferatu hideousness. &quot;Oh no! They can see that I'm... bald!&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-06T00:48:56-07:00","id":1560404,"title":"","content":"Brian Thompson is never a waste of time watching.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-06T01:51:45-07:00","id":1560405,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502231-feel-free-to-gush?p=1560400#post1560400\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Rokea weren't specifically noted as being ageless until the 2nd edition player's guide. One of those &quot;what do you mean we didn't mention that?&quot; things.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I disagree; the actor allusions alone would be hilarious in a riff show. Sasha was played by the same actress that portrayed Thina in Quest of the Delta Knights, Brian Thompson (who was in almost everything) was Eddie Fiori, and as for Sonny, well, Surprise, Motherfucker!<br /> <br /> There's also the obligatory jokes about Nosferatu hideousness. &quot;Oh no! They can see that I'm... bald!&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Which vampire show was it, that made it obvious they didn't understand the source material?<br /> <br /> Because the only thing I remember about it, is that they depicted the Brujah as behaving like Ventrue, and the Gangrel as behaving like Brujah.<br /> <br /> I also think the show did so poorly, it was canceled after a few episodes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-06T08:43:03-07:00","id":1560407,"title":"","content":"I might be in the minority, but I loved Kindred the Embraced. Was it as faithful to the source material as it could have been? No... but it was all the had at the time! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I watched it when it aired, and my gaming group in college would get together each week and watch it. It was awesome watching a show based on the game we were actively playing.<br /> <br /> For what it is, I still think it's pretty fun. Maybe someday they'll do a new show based on VtM that's a little more faithful the game..<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkKing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502231-feel-free-to-gush?p=1560405#post1560405\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I also think the show did so poorly, it was canceled after a few episodes.</div> </div> </div> </div>It ran it's full season. I believe it got canceled after season 1 aired, or just didn't get renewed. The actor whole played Julian Luna, Mark Finkel, died in traffic accident I think, but I don't think that played a part in the cancellation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/\" target=\"_blank\">MrGone's Character Sheets</a><br /> For all your WoD Character Sheet Needs<br /> _________________________________<br /> Buy books &amp; pdfs from DTRPG and support my web site! <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=55414\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a><br /> Support my site on Patreon! <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mrgone\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a>","edited":{"userid":24,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24-mr-gone","user":"Mr Gone","date":". 06-06-2026, 11:46 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24-mr-gone","name":"Mr Gone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-06T09:25:15-07:00","id":1560408,"title":"","content":"While Mark's death wasn't the reason the show's continuation came into question, it was likely the tipping point since his performance was largely seen as the saving grace of the show for general audiences that were struggling with not knowing the VtM lore, and VtM fans struggling with how different things got in adaptation. The buzz from back in the day was definitely that the show as in trouble, and that pushed Fox and Spelling into dropping the show with the ability to make it less about strict finances and more about a reasonable case that without their lead actor it was going to be too hard to put the show on a stronger footing in future seasons.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-06T10:35:59-07:00","id":1560410,"title":"","content":"The show had a few well known actors and actresses. We had C. Thomas Howell, Brian Thompson, Kelly Rutherford and Jeff Korber and I usually enjoy seeing them in most cases.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-06T14:08:51-07:00","id":1560413,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502231-feel-free-to-gush?p=1560408#post1560408\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The buzz from back in the day was definitely that the show as in trouble, and that pushed Fox and Spelling into dropping the show with the ability to make it less about strict finances and more about a reasonable case that without their lead actor it was going to be too hard to put the show on a stronger footing in future seasons.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Oh, FOX was involved? That explains it!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-07T05:13:26-07:00","id":1560430,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502231-feel-free-to-gush?p=1560408#post1560408\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While Mark's death wasn't the reason the show's continuation came into question, it was likely the tipping point since his performance was largely seen as the saving grace of the show for general audiences that were struggling with not knowing the VtM lore, and VtM fans struggling with how different things got in adaptation. The buzz from back in the day was definitely that the show as in trouble, and that pushed Fox and Spelling into dropping the show with the ability to make it less about strict finances and more about a reasonable case that without their lead actor it was going to be too hard to put the show on a stronger footing in future seasons.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, that does make sense. He was definitely the best thing about the show. I liked that character a lot, and even used him in a game back in the day. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/\" target=\"_blank\">MrGone's Character Sheets</a><br /> For all your WoD Character Sheet Needs<br /> _________________________________<br /> Buy books &amp; pdfs from DTRPG and support my web site! <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=55414\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a><br /> Support my site on Patreon! <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mrgone\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24-mr-gone","name":"Mr Gone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-07T23:25:59-07:00","id":1560447,"title":"","content":"It's always good when you see the next generation of fans getting into the IP that you were into when you were that age and if you help out at bookstore like me, you can recommend creative runs that you enjoyed and see if they will enjoy them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-08T01:53:27-07:00","id":1560449,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr Gone</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502231-feel-free-to-gush?p=1560407#post1560407\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I might be in the minority, but I loved Kindred the Embraced. Was it as faithful to the source material as it could have been? No... but it was all the had at the time! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>The <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=A-_-8D8R4CU\" target=\"_blank\">BattleTech cartoon</a> is close to a lot of people for much the same reason, but it eventually got retconned into being FedCom G.I Joe (a children's war propaganda cartoon within the setting, to match being a not particularly accurate show about the setting IRL). It even has some crazy lore links, too, like one of the Jade Falcon warriors portrayed in the show attempted to take legal action regarding his portrayal (and then attempting to issue a challenge of combat to the judge, which... did not work, given he was attempting action in Steiner territory), and some characters in a fiction piece of Wars of Reaving laughing at how it was essentially the purest form of cringe to them (as warriors of Clan Wolf) to the point that they found it hilarious.<br /> <br /> And now we have <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=oqbKv4HomFA\" target=\"_blank\">this</a>!<br /> <br /> The cartoon also had some notable voice talent; Adam Steiner's voice would eventually get Hollywood famous to some degree (he went on to be Reich in Ravenous and M. Bison in SF: The Legend of Chun-li), Jennifer Darling was playing double duty as the 1SS adjutant and Star Colonel Kristen Redmond, the voice of Franklin Sakamoto was Leonardo in the Ninja Turtles live action movies (suit and voice work), Cpt. Hawkins was portrayed by the late Peter Spellos (you may also remember him for his work in anime dubbing and... that crazed chef in Munchie that chased after the flying pizza), and Jennifer Hale had a brief role as Archon Melissa Steiner (two conversations in the beginning of the series!).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-08T08:31:23-07:00","id":1560456,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502231-feel-free-to-gush?p=1560449#post1560449\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=A-_-8D8R4CU\" target=\"_blank\">BattleTech cartoon</a> is close to a lot of people for much the same reason, but it eventually got retconned into being FedCom G.I Joe (a children's war propaganda cartoon within the setting, to match being a not particularly accurate show about the setting IRL). It even has some crazy lore links, too, like one of the Jade Falcon warriors portrayed in the show attempted to take legal action regarding his portrayal (and then attempting to issue a challenge of combat to the judge, which... did not work, given he was attempting action in Steiner territory), and some characters in a fiction piece of Wars of Reaving laughing at how it was essentially the purest form of cringe to them (as warriors of Clan Wolf) to the point that they found it hilarious.<br /> <br /> And now we have <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=oqbKv4HomFA\" target=\"_blank\">this</a>!<br /> <br /> The cartoon also had some notable voice talent; Adam Steiner's voice would eventually get Hollywood famous to some degree (he went on to be Reich in Ravenous and M. Bison in SF: The Legend of Chun-li), Jennifer Darling was playing double duty as the 1SS adjutant and Star Colonel Kristen Redmond, the voice of Franklin Sakamoto was Leonardo in the Ninja Turtles live action movies (suit and voice work), Cpt. Hawkins was portrayed by the late Peter Spellos (you may also remember him for his work in anime dubbing and... that crazed chef in Munchie that chased after the flying pizza), and Jennifer Hale had a brief role as Archon Melissa Steiner (two conversations in the beginning of the series!).</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh whoa. I remember Battle Tech form back in the day, but never got as into it as other stuff, so I had no idea about some of this. Crazy! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/\" target=\"_blank\">MrGone's Character Sheets</a><br /> For all your WoD Character Sheet Needs<br /> _________________________________<br /> Buy books &amp; pdfs from DTRPG and support my web site! <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=55414\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a><br /> Support my site on Patreon! <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mrgone\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24-mr-gone","name":"Mr Gone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-08T11:18:42-07:00","id":1560459,"title":"","content":"I remember Battletech back in the day, but it came on very early in the morning where I lived and I didn't get a chance to see much of the series, but we have novels based in the universe that I intend to read.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"a