nt":"Space Ice reviewed/roasted \ud83c\udf60 the original Masters of the Universe movie and I forgot how much of a guilty pleasure that movie is with Frank Langella and Meg Foster being the best things in the film and I forgot that Anthony Delongis was in the film and he played the Blade character and served as Langella stunt double for the action scenes.<br /> <br /> I remember Delongis from Highlander as the one of the people who handled the sword fighting scenes and was on a espoide of Deadliest Warrior showing how powerful and effective a Claymore is in the right hands on the William Wallace vs Shaka Zulu battle.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-10T00:11:07-07:00","id":1562929,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502231-feel-free-to-gush?p=1562923#post1562923\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I remember Delongis from Highlander as the one of the people who handled the sword fighting scenes and was on a espoide of Deadliest Warrior showing how powerful and effective a Claymore is in the right hands on the William Wallace vs Shaka Zulu battle.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I was bewildered when the Zulu representative actually claimed that a shield made of wood and cow hide would be able to stop a steel claymore. Then laughed when the simulated battle had him chop straight through it in one swing.<br /> <br /> Also, sending a practically naked Zulu warrior into battle against a man clad in full body armor seems kind of one sided. I don't know who was responsible for organizing that vs match, but they need to choose better matchups.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-10T00:33:34-07:00","id":1562930,"title":"","content":"When they were doing Deadliest Warrior they wanted to do all sorts of match ups and show case the weapons, tactics and how they train and how well they would do in a simulated match up <br /> <br /> I had no problem with it at all. The Zulu would have difficulty using the claymore as they have no training with it and the Scottish warriors wouldn't be able to use the weapons of the Zulu effectively either.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-10T04:09:48-07:00","id":1562939,"title":"","content":"I barely remember the old MotU movie, but for some reason I didn't like it back then. My guess is that I was expecting Gorpo maybe more than I should, I really liked him as a kid.<br /> <br /> Deadliest Warriors is barely better than a scam, I hope you all know. It used a lot of dubious tech to give an appearance of serious research, but it was actually full of holes. It's fun, but don't take anything there as representative of reality.<br /> <br /> As for Shaka Zulu, he was not an exceptional warrior, but exceptional tactician and shrewd diplomat. His innovations on Zulu warfare led to a strong army that managed to impose heavy defeats upon the Dutch and British in the 19th century even decades after his death. But his political maneuvers were generally more impressive.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-10T04:30:00-07:00","id":1562942,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502231-feel-free-to-gush?p=1562939#post1562939\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for Shaka Zulu, he was not an exceptional warrior, but exceptional tactician and shrewd diplomat. His innovations on Zulu warfare led to a strong army that managed to impose heavy defeats upon the Dutch and British in the 19th century even decades after his death. But his political maneuvers were generally more impressive.</div> </div> </div> </div>I heard that when the Europeans introduced him to the invention of hair dye, he bought as much of it as he could, because he mistook it for an elixir of youth.<br /> <br /> Also, he was killed by his own family, because he started going completely insane and was making decisions that put his people on the path towards inevitable destruction.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-10T04:50:47-07:00","id":1562945,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkKing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502231-feel-free-to-gush?p=1562942#post1562942\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I heard that when the Europeans introduced him to the invention of hair dye, he bought as much of it as he could, because he mistook it for an elixir of youth.<br /> <br /> Also, he was killed by his own family, because he started going completely insane and was making decisions that put his people on the path towards inevitable destruction.</div> </div> </div> </div>The first is invention, the second is uncertain, but probably an exaggeration.<br /> <br /> His half brothers were attempting to murder him for some time to take control over the Zulu kingdom, and actual records of the time are few, this story mostly came from the brother who took the kingdom and spent the following decade trying to get rid of Shaka's loyalists.<br /> <br /> A lot of myths surround Shaka because of the lack of written records among the Zulu and the Europeans that did write something being the creative rather than accurate types.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":5826,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","user":"monteparnas","date":". 08-10-2026, 11:53 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-10T05:00:39-07:00","id":1562946,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502231-feel-free-to-gush?p=1562945#post1562945\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> A lot of myths surround Shaka because of the black of written records among the Zulu and the Europeans that did write something being the creative rather than accurate types.</div> </div> </div> </div>Let's hope the &quot;year of mourning&quot; was a fabrication then, because reading about that is just absurd.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-10T08:56:53-07:00","id":1562959,"title":"","content":"I do remember the espoide of Spartan vs Ninja and thinking that doesn't sound right as Spartans fought and trained as a unit and wouldn't likely to fight one on one as it wasn't there way of warfare and I enjoyed the show.. Also ninjas weren't typically front lines soliders as I recall.<br /> <br /> The History Channel did a better job on History Deadliest Warriors and how they were trained and how they came to be and why some of them died out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-10T08:59:31-07:00","id":1562960,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkKing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502231-feel-free-to-gush?p=1562946#post1562946\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Let's hope the &quot;year of mourning&quot; was a fabrication then, because reading about that is just absurd.</div> </div> </div> </div>It most probably is. And is far from the only of the type in history. Kings and emperors all around faced similar situations, from Rome to China and beyond both.<br /> <br /> At least half of the absurds we &quot;know&quot; about emperors like Caligula and Nero are slander by enemies or later authors with political agendas, for example, even if not everything.<br /> <br /> Given how Zulu politics worked at the time and that Shaka himself used similar tactics against enemies, I think it at least slightly more likely than not that the Year of Mourning was at least severely exaggerated.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-10T09:08:51-07:00","id":1562962,"title":"","content":"Yes how much about Caligula being mad was mostly political propaganda written after his death and be mindful that there's lots about the classical age that we are in the dark about because of wars, natural disasters and political purging.<br /> <br /> And your not alone Montparnasse about the original Masters of the Universe movie being disliked as it didn't look or feel like what we saw in the cartoon or the various comics. <br /> <br /> I like it because you could see how low the budget was for the movie and even for a Cannon Films production it was bad.<br /> <br /> Even Frank Langella and Meg Foster superb acting skills were not enough to make the film profitable.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude02","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-10T10:41:27-07:00","id":1562968,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502231-feel-free-to-gush?p=1562959#post1562959\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I do remember the espoide of Spartan vs Ninja and thinking that doesn't sound right as Spartans fought and trained as a unit and wouldn't likely to fight one on one as it wasn't there way of warfare and I enjoyed the show.. Also ninjas weren't typically front lines soliders as I recall.<br /> <br /> The History Channel did a better job on History Deadliest Warriors and how they were trained and how they came to be and why some of them died out.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ninjas weren't even warriors, actually. They were more like spies and infiltrators. That's actually what the term <i>&quot;shinobi&quot;</i> translates to <i>&quot;Preserving Stealth Person.&quot;</i><br /> <br /> With the exception of their assassination target, a ninja avoided killing unless it was absolutely necessary. Because racking up a body count would alert the guards to your presence.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-10T13:08:47-07:00","id":1562975,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkKing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1502231-feel-free-to-gush?p=1562968#post1562968\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ninjas weren't even warriors, actually. They were more like spies and infiltrators. That's actually what the term <i>&quot;shinobi&quot;</i> translates to <i>&quot;Preserving Stealth Person.&quot;</i><br /> <br /> With the exception of their assassination target, a ninja avoided killing unless it was absolutely necessary. Because racking up a body count would alert the guards to your presence.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sometimes, sometimes not.<br /> <br /> The word <i>shinobi</i> was used for a number of activities, from infiltration to scouts to simpler informants.<br /> <br /> <i>Ninja</i> is usually used for the Iga and K\u014dga when they formed their independent territory for a time during the sengoku. Those were actually warriors, guerilla fighters to be precise with a lot of experience in the mountains. But while their exploits at the time were a major inspiration for later ninja legendry, they were not professional spies, just some mercenary jizamurai with a good grasp of their lands.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-10T14:15:38-07:00","id":1562978,"title":"","content":"Ninjas were many things during their time in the &quot;spotlight&quot; so to speak. Warriors, Scouts, Assassin and experts in psychology.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-10T15:34:41-07:00","id":1562985,"title":"","content":"One of Space Ice roasts on the original Masters of the Universe was about how poor the security around Castle Greyskull is as both He-Man and Skeletors forces could get in easily and claim squatters rights.<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-10T17:49:44-07:00","id":1562994,"title":"","content":"Shinobi is the original word that existed since the 8th century and saw most historical use.<br /> <br /> Ninja is an on'y\u014dmi, a &quot;Chinese version&quot; for the word that developed in the 12th century but is specific for training schools based on guerilla tactics.<br /> <br /> For the following centuries we can say that the word Ninja refers to the person trained in one such guerilla school and it's a budding trade, but the archetype and word most used is still shinobi. Which also means ninja are limited in scope to guerilla, and they'll actually remain like that.<br /> <br /> By the 15th century we reach the Sengoku, and ninja schools see more use. They're not a class in itself, even though there are families/clans that sustain proprietary schools. Most ninjas are samurai, though not all. Non-ninja Shinobi still exist and are uses, too, so the archetype is not yet &quot;renamed&quot;.<br /> <br /> What established the foundation of the modern ninja archetype was the independence of Iga province and K\u014dka district. Those were areas run by jizamurai, peasants with military training for local protection. Due to local geography, the communities managed by the end of the 15th century to drive away the war lords and remain independent, but their guerilla tactics, mastery of local geography and neutrality made them a new level of favored mercs.<br /> <br /> The K\u014dga remained independent for 89 years, the Iga lasted 8 years more, then Nobunaga got their lands and they joined Tokugawa. Not long after that Tokugawa would establish the new Shogunate and end the Sengoku, and this is a fundamental pivot. Among many reforms, Tokugawa has a thorough plan for the cultural transformation of Japan, that relies a lot on the romanticization of the Sengoku.<br /> <br /> He established with a combination of reforms, propaganda and theater patronage the whole modern conceptualization of the period. And it included many, many plays about his allies in the Iga and K\u014dga, and their mysterious villages hidden in the mountains. <i><b>Those plays</b></i> are what finally formulate and enshrined the archetype of the Ninja, and start to apply to it attributes from Shinobi more deeply.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-10T19:24:43-07:00","id":1562999,"title":"","content":"You ever read the Secret History of Ninjas? It covers many of the same points you brought up.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&